// AUTOMATISCH gebaut aus lang/src/en/*.txt mit: node tools/i18n-bau.js – nicht von Hand ändern.
window.LANGS=window.LANGS||{};LANGS.en={"13thqhr":"Error:","ux28qq":"(line","1i2r6d5":"Swamp of the","13osbww":"Drowned Harlots","1zeca2":"To the forest path","2hdvte":"To the swamp","1jeoxoa":"To the fisherman's hut","1jsv4p2":"To the crossroads","1g8ttyw":"To the dark forest","m66nkt":"To the shore","197rw1q":"To the old mill","o0byto":"Into the village","locnzl":"To Baba Yaga","vny8bq":"To the church","1dkn39a":"To the smithy","zvuacj":"To the village gate","1chuz0t":"Back to the village","pkzoi3":"A stick... some string... and for a hook, a safety pin from my trousers.","u1c8ls":"Behold, a fishing rod. If my father could see me now... he'd be ashamed. As usual.","r3cz1v":"Oh. I actually caught one. A real fish. Who'd have thought.","1x3o0ta":"That's a tiddler. I'd have thrown it back. Or gaffer-taped it to the bait.","ydhzdp":"It's for a cat, not for you.","cqp9th":"*crack* ...And the rod's done for. Held exactly one fish. As advertised.","ghgyzo":"Gone. The fish has more muscle than I do.","3pfp6m":"Again! And pull back, boy! Like dancing with my first wife. She kept slipping off the hook too.","7hw7rv":"It's breaking loose! Pull against it!","14ucdw8":"Keep the float inside the circle – the fish is pulling the other way!","1i8hjya":"[Give up]","14wf36e":"Under the pier","17zgw4y":"To the gnome village","1avixvc":"Back to the shore","1ufdr8j":"Wait for the bite... Only click when it REALLY pulls!","awfam2":"Gave up.","174l9qr":"Pulled too early too often. The catfish no longer trusts the worms.","pu84vb":"Hit! He's getting tired...","13kpyxx":"The catfish tore free with the last of its strength.","1pybbof":"(from above) WHAT?! It's pulling! IT'S PULLING! That's HIM! THE CATFISH! Hold, line, I gaffer-taped you myself!","rj6fd9":"Come here, you slimy bastard! Thirty years I've waited! Thirty years patching this rod with tape!","vsglf8":"Perfect. That'll keep him busy for a while.","zhrfsv":"And his bottle is standing all alone on the pier...","1rh129k":"Again. There are still a few worms wriggling on there.","hq8bbc":"Missed the bite five times. The catfish ate the worms and left.","1l1r19d":"SNAP! Pulled too hard – the line broke.","hhsmi":"Too slack! The catfish spat out the worms.","15fx5fp":"He's tiring! Click exactly when the ring touches the circle!","137dra7":"Tension","1i1t2kt":"HE'S PULLING!","3p0cnm":"Catfish strength","ac61z5":"Phase 1: The bite","1kw8rub":"Phase 3: Wear him out","4b25j2":"Toad + Moon","1dpd9pc":"Pull the filter off the joint and drop it in the \"Filter\" box.","1l32ko":"Unrolled! Now put the paper in the \"Paper\" box.","9v0s37":"Now unroll the paper: drag across the joint from left to right.","1oa9rs6":"Sort the blue-tinged mushroom bits into the bowl. Only those! (Mistakes: 0/3)","1a18g5k":"That's a perfectly normal button mushroom!","p9d7fn":"That's tobacco!","1rg57hf":"The bowl is contaminated! Sort it all again. (Mistakes: 0/3)","jzwxs4":"Nine pieces. All of them blue. These are not normal mushrooms.","hh4x9k":"Bring them here, layabout. Let old Yaga sniff your bloody merchandise.","6pc7nb":"Later. My fingers don't feel like it today.","1jgn7x2":"Paper","1vvvdef":"Filter","1j20soj":"Bowl","1283euf":"Step 1/4: Filter off","w4hmpl":"Step 2/4: Unroll","bfj5ui":"Step 3/4: Paper away","1v18iet":"[Later]","14qkmy3":"To the cave","13q541o":"To the garden","ym912b":"To the exit","tr7o53":"Saturday. No money, no job, no plan. Perfect.","1xq3a3g":"*takes a drag* ...This stuff used to be better.","y9ilfk":"Petya! Bro! You still smoking that garden rubbish? That's compost, mate, you get me?","1gdqo8r":"Vova. How did you get in?","19io097":"Door was open, as usual. Right, listen, listen: I've got something. Brand new. Proper mental, you get me?","1ydffo":"Granny's herbs, bro! Got 'em off a bloke at the market. Mad eyes. And webbed fingers. Whatever! You're having me on if you care!","jb4elq":"He says one puff and you're in another world! Fairyland, you get me?! Not winding you up!","13v9gmy":"Sounds like trouble.","c5v1zn":"Sounds like Saturday, bro!","1oqwfbr":"...Fine. Hand it over.","kss0v3":"*inhales*","1tr6dzz":"*cough* ...*COUGH*","b9hbtg":"Well? Well?! Is it kicking in? Say something – is it working or is it rubbish gear?","14ae1c6":"Vova... why... do you have three noses?","1blar1s":"Bro? ...BRO?! You having me on?!","10ljq2l":"Uhhh... my head...","12cchjk":"Where am I? This isn't my flat. My flat has fewer... birches.","1iz79rf":"Vova's joint. He said it had \"Granny's herbs\" in it. Whose granny? ...Of course this happens to me.","12o37oc":"Marvellous. So I just have to wake up somehow.","161rqxb":"M I L L","9nehzo":"To the village","sxhzey":"Into the Maze Wood","14ifkpa":"Left","1633gpu":"Right","19vetx2":"Straight on","rwnkr9":"Back to the mill","1otboma":"Steam · Dance · Vodka","v179ji":"To the mill","1ygz6rt":"NO SHOW TODAY","qakzth":"Outside","1vhz2mq":"Dance? Sweetie, I've had this whole swamp wrapped round my little finger. With my hips. The frogs have croaked differently ever since. Tee-hee!","55bu73":"Out? YES! Down here the only thing that touches you is reeds. And they are not gentle. Unlike some.","1nqo6gl":"You? You smell of smoke and panic. But you look at me like a cat looks at cream. I like that, gorgeous.","kuomun":"Dance? I danced at merchants' weddings until the tables broke. And the marriages. Tee-hee, especially the marriages.","scj9n8":"Out? Pff. Down here I'm the queen. Out there I'm just a wet woman with a past. Like Fyokla, but pretty.","1rzmhrv":"Cute puppy. Come closer, I only bite if you ask nicely. Girls, look at him!","12wv326":"Prima ballerina, 1903! ...All right, the knees are mud now. Marfa's were mud back then.","1wyomcv":"Oh yes! I want an audience again! Applause! Flowers! So this lot turn green with envy. Greener.","19bd0wo":"Young man, you smell like the dregs of a vodka bottle. Charming. Tee-hee.","1dcjxtg":"Dance? I can barely turn around. *blub* The girls are laughing. Let them.","1fupbdg":"Out? I've been marinating here. Nobody's getting me out now. Except for gossip.","z8wqfx":"You stink. And I'm a drowned corpse. So: respect. Tee-hee.","1kivfxs":"No. I'd sooner punch than dance.","zf3n1v":"Out! And then I find whoever drowned me. And his wife. And her sister.","m79d72":"Shut it, greenhorn, or I'll drag you under. The girls would love that.","18aenwy":"*rattle* I dance the bone dance. Every night. Alone. These tarts never invite me.","psczvg":"Out? Where to? I've been everywhere. Dead.","aema6q":"*rattle* ...Pretty boy. Pretty meaty. Tee-hee.","cl8er0":"Can you dance?","1i6w4zr":"Do you want out of the swamp?","1t58xou":"What do you think of me?","1wevglz":"Conversation","1kmtjdr":"Ask her something.","10wz1e":"Trait card","4r3ltt":"Pretty","5xy826":"Loves to dance","7v8si4":"Cheeky / crude","d2903u":"Wants out","1b1zhlh":"Recruit","ykyzv0":"Back","1mj8xbs":"[ESC] close","1c5a7o6":"Hm. I think I misjudged her. The card's wrong.","19f1ghv":"The card is right. But she doesn't fit Madame's list.","1q1uy83":"Nastya... fancy a job? Dancing. Music. Vodka. A place without frogs.","dtgphc":"A job? A stage, an audience, tips? Darling, I'm already on my way. Just wringing out my hair – then the boys can start paying.","1609nqb":"The banya is beyond the Maze Wood. Tell them Petya sent you.","9cds70":"...Madame will be pleased. And hopefully so will I.","1sfmnxg":"Back to the club","kcysig":"Welcome to the lounge, gorgeous. Sit. Hands on the sofa – you touch with your eyes. Nothing's free, darling.","1oifmtu":"I... er... yes. Sofa. Hands. Got it.","mjs3jz":"And now... music, sweetheart!","ho911t":"*Three minutes later*","1go5xcy":"I think I need a vodka. Or two. Or a cold shower in the swamp.","igtiz9":"Come back soon, Petya darling. And bring your wallet – I miss it already.","1qfrgfs":"Back to the bar","o0b4oz":"Hands on the sofa, gorgeous. Looking's free. For now.","1e1cfq2":"*gulp*","q87ds7":"*sniff* ...What... what is this? My eyes! My mascara, damn it!","18p60yk":"*SNIFF* I'm crying! I never cry! Three hundred years without a single tear, and now this!","r4zf36":"Hold still. *holds the vial under her chin*","1df7poy":"*plop* A real tear. Thank you.","18npvuk":"*laughing through tears* An onion. You cheeky little sod, you stuck an onion in the vent.","12q22t6":"Three hundred years and no man ever made me cry. You did it with a vegetable. Now that's what I call an approach.","pigwr7":"Keep the tear, Onion. You've earned it. First one's free. Nothing else is.","ek89a9":"(I think she likes me. In a nymph sort of way.)","lwbfd2":"...I think I need a vodka. Or two. Or a cold shower in the swamp.","1ekfvsn":"Come back soon, Petya darling. But next time with a tip. Nothing's free, sweetheart.","1i4xm6l":"The path splits. Of course. In fairytales the path always splits.","7dyft8":"And there's a sign. At least somebody here is organised.","1n8rdu1":"There it is. A hut on chicken legs.","t4xerd":"Vova, if I ever get out of here, I'm going to kill you.","a558v0":"Who's that creeping round my house? I smell city air! Some layabout!","14ao7z0":"A swamp. It stinks of rot and... perfume?","1ajd2zg":"There are naked women sitting in the water. Sure. Why not. Don't stare, Petya.","1j0h7lt":"...Some of them are over a hundred. Okay, now I'm staring for different reasons.","1906qv7":"A lake. And a fisherman. Finally someone who isn't naked or standing on chicken legs.","ugjvws":"Well, with that beard you never know.","c5abu9":"A village. With houses. And even electricity.","1ugupy9":"...No. The wires are just hanging about.","1lqets4":"A shop, a well, a church and a burnt-down house. Classic village.","wdocka":"Lovely. Birches everywhere. As if someone dumped them here on purpose.","ko4heh":"And left and right nothing but forest. Thick as a wall. And dark as the inside of a bear.","wizpe3":"Without a saw I'm not getting through there.","gsjh88":"Right at the front of the stage. From here you can see... everything. The choreography, I mean.","xixvak":"The Maze Wood. Three paths, all identical. And something is staring at me from the dark.","18rsnuz":"A log cabin in the middle of the darkest forest. Red light, music, steam from the chimney. Naturally.","zp7ii7":"That must be the banya. It's so dark out here even the owls are scared.","1b495vj":"The banya. Steam, red light, the smell of vodka. And a stage with a curtain.","l822d9":"New face! Come in, sweetie. Wipe your feet, keep your trousers on, loosen your wallet. In that order.","1j9lwff":"An old watermill. The wheel turns, the water rushes.","1mwmqvr":"And nobody's here. Who switched the thing on? Water... fine. But still.","143vpwf":"A settlement. Round huts, a fence, a smell of cabbage behind it... and there are gnomes.","lxx07m":"Big gnomes. Very big gnomes. With very, very big noses.","1vnf0v5":"A cave. Cold, damp and something's dripping somewhere.","12lcjde":"Glowing mushrooms, crystals, an underground lake. And at the back a tunnel into pitch black.","79wndt":"Well, look at that! A guest through the window. As is proper, smart-arse!","1fcucvx":"You reek of smoke, layabout. And something else... Turn out your bloody pockets.","1x8lkm5":"Just an old joint stub.","1gnzixs":"Put it on the table and take it apart. I don't touch that bloody joint. Gout.","1932dus":"The shore. Reeds, mud and a boat that gave up long ago.","1datpfn":"Up ahead the pier begins. Underneath it's dark. Of course.","19caznt":"Under the pier. It smells of algae, fish and Kuzmich's feet.","1o8kc22":"His line hangs down through the planks. Empty hook. No wonder nothing ever bites.","125oxbu":"The village street. Sunflowers, washing lines, chicken muck. Almost cosy.","rzg671":"There's a church at the back. And a granny peering over her garden gate. They always peer.","bnd27v":"A wooden church with onion domes. And a graveyard with blue railings.","1imlo07":"A fat black cat is squatting on that grave. It's staring at me. I stare back. It wins.","390xme":"To the path","9g9ijs":"To the birch forest","1d80x1j":"Petya","1g35d77":"Crow","rjuwe6":"Sun","1n9smtc":"Toadstool","1s1vulm":"Birch","1jm3x4p":"Voice from the hut","1w3le7o":"Mila","iw5iww":"Vera","eogoe9":"Dunya","bldnzs":"Kuzmich the Fisherman","4a3lb1":"Granny Dusya","1i1l4a6":"Madame Zinaida","154ms6":"Voice from the mill","z0g0b6":"Mushroom Master Bulb","1itfzoi":"Marfa","1sw2gsy":"Nastya","1ofkffj":"Vova","esam79":"Grobnik","1hgu17x":"Grandpa Snobbel","t1lszy":"Baba Yaga","1xr3opw":"Grandpa Grisha","g44bkd":"If I get out of here, I'm never smoking anything again. ...Hardly ever.","1j0xfjc":"Hello? Player? I'm just standing here.","1jfksf6":"My feet have gone to sleep. Lucky them.","v5ugiz":"I'm hungry. For pelmeni. Or anything that doesn't talk back.","10iixig":"Mum always said I'd never amount to anything. Now I'm in a fairytale. ...Well. It's something.","zpese4":"If I stand still long enough, maybe I'll just wake up.","19k47or":"I'll count to three and everything will be normal. One... two... Nope. Still fairytale.","1jskk8e":"Somewhere out there my body is lying on a sofa. Hopefully with a blanket.","4zsue3":"Brilliant. Standing in a forest waiting for a miracle. Like every Saturday.","8826k":"Of course this happens to me. Who else.","1subx3m":"Will anyone notice I'm gone? ...Probably not. Doesn't matter. ...It doesn't.","tn2sbm":"Mum always rings on Sundays. ...Hope somebody picks up. Whatever. Moving on.","1kwzafy":"If this is a dream, it's badly written.","1xoj07p":"I could be doing something useful right now. Could.","1cj7m55":"I've still got my keys. Not that they help here.","qwbate":"Vova owes me. At least a beer. More like a life.","sbniml":"Short break. I've earned it. I think.","1p8f6ah":"No signal on my phone. In a fairytale. Who'd have guessed.","151j59g":"If I tell anyone about this, nobody'll believe me. Just as well, really.","194bpo0":"I'm waiting. I'm good at waiting. Years of practice.","cue10m":"I miss my sofa a bit. And the fridge. The empty one.","1mcmt4e":"If one more mushroom winks at me, I'm leaving.","1c6ol5s":"My gran would've loved it here. She liked weird people.","5t58v0":"These birches are whispering about me. I can hear it.","l2c4a7":"Yesterday this was my living room. I think.","4jfeu4":"I swear that toadstool just winked at me.","134fcml":"Lots of forest. Not much exit.","s5n764":"The crow looks like it's running a betting pool on me.","1rz13x5":"This is where it all started. And I didn't even take a photo.","1wm7szu":"Left, right, straight on. Everything feels wrong.","fup6hb":"A signpost would be nice. One that doesn't lie.","18jcbzv":"Three paths. And they all want something from me.","1h4buky":"If I don't decide, I can't decide wrong. Genius.","1l570su":"A house on chicken legs. Perfectly normal. Totally normal.","bp8ef1":"If the hut starts running, I'm running with it.","bsgb6":"The skulls on the fence are grinning. At least someone's in a good mood.","15m1k76":"The hut just yawned. I'm imagining it. ...Definitely.","w8bmso":"Smells of cabbage and magic. Mostly cabbage.","e9kc0m":"Everything in here smells of herbs and bad decisions.","jlqcsm":"I'd better not touch anything. Except maybe the pirozhki.","1ejg50e":"Something moved on the shelf. I'm not looking.","p1pzg6":"Cosy. For a witch. Less so for me.","1czzofu":"Loud music, red light. Almost like home on a Friday.","12lzi3g":"Stay cool, Petya. Hands in your pockets.","1x3aexe":"I'm only looking. For cultural reasons.","1mjczxp":"I... should probably just leave. Soon. Eventually.","5qacmy":"This is my third time here. Or my first. Three times.","1ifi967":"The trees are standing differently from before. I swear.","1mscic8":"If I starve to death here, no eulogy, please.","1pn1ftk":"I should have left a trail of breadcrumbs. The crow would've eaten them anyway.","11p66nl":"Red light in the woods. You don't see that every day.","44r43a":"The bass is thumping inside. Eyes are glowing out in the woods. I'll go in, thanks.","1ow2wes":"I'm standing outside a club in an enchanted forest. My life has taken a very odd turn.","kk7pgg":"Steam, birch twigs, vodka. Finally a place I understand.","bup1dt":"Watching makes me thirsty.","1m7vmye":"The music is bad. But loud. It evens out.","1xlj96u":"If Vova could see this. He'd be a regular by tonight.","jeog48":"A village. With people. ...Hopefully with people.","1eazeji":"Someone here must have kvass. I just have to ask.","6f8b6v":"Nothing has happened here since 1991. And then I turned up.","hfneio":"Power lines with no power. I know the feeling. I live in a flat like that.","1o538fg":"People are looking at me like I'm the weird one here.","1hrsdr5":"Smells of smoke and cabbage soup. Like Gran's.","1n0q35w":"A pair of underpants as a sail. Nothing goes to waste here.","t6dpo9":"The chickens here have more self-esteem than I do.","cvbi94":"Shhh, Petya. No swearing in here.","jqhsp5":"If anyone here needs a miracle, it's me.","1in7qvf":"The cat's staring at me. I stare back. It wins. Again.","1v3p3zv":"Graveyards are pretty relaxing, actually. Nobody talks. Mostly.","1wmj6lu":"The mill is creaking. Or is that my back?","6w63bk":"Flour everywhere. I look like a ghost. A hungry one.","a0tzti":"The waterwheel is turning. I'll be turning too in a minute. Just from watching.","medym1":"Someone's breathing behind the door. Heavily. And shyly.","ks4klr":"Who knocked the birches over? Wasn't me. I think.","z0lwv6":"I'll never shift that with my bare hands.","1phnd92":"Dark here. So dark I can't even see my own laziness.","zh2by6":"Something's rustling in the undergrowth. I'll call it Kevin. Then it's less scary.","1yvi2fu":"Don't stare. Don't stare. ...Damn.","o54xff":"If I sink in here, nobody's coming to look for me.","18pj27j":"It's bubbling. I hope that was the swamp.","3cn3ap":"My socks are wet. And that's the most normal thing here.","1r9df8c":"Fish smell. I think it lives in my jacket now.","15x82ru":"A fisherman with no boat. A Petya with no plan. We're a match.","8hus7a":"Kuzmich hasn't caught anything since 1987. I feel seen.","yfmmns":"The lake is sparkling. The only one here making an effort.","i3rlyv":"The water's so calm. Far too calm.","yt38k9":"If I jump in now, at least I'll be awake.","1uge524":"Reeds, mud, silence. Sounds like a bad spa weekend.","fwldgv":"Dark, wet, and something's dripping down my collar.","13j1rxp":"Nobody can hear me scream down here. Good to know.","1mtzq8y":"Kuzmich creaks above me. The pier creaks below me. I'll be creaking too soon.","1xbf9mp":"Everything's so small here. I feel like a giant. A tired giant.","1utuvkw":"I hope the gnomes don't bite. They've got that look.","7lhhit":"Giant cabbages and giant noses. Everything here is a size too big. Except the people.","1g7eydv":"Pipe smoke and cabbage. Just like my uncle's.","1mzzdjp":"Mushrooms on the walls. Wonderful. Exactly my problem.","140vq1k":"Echo. ...Echo? No answer. Not even the echo likes me.","tdp5r0":"The crystals are humming. Hopefully not Radio Moscow.","1k5qdxl":"Cold in here. And something's giggling somewhere. Perfectly normal cave.","1mttexb":"Back at the start. Doesn't feel like progress.","13qv0jl":"The birch forest. Still smells of my mistake.","946itk":"Hello, crow. Miss me? No? Thought not.","18rwoej":"The crossroads. I'm starting to know my way around. Worrying, really.","3oulcr":"Back again. Hopefully the signs are still lying the same way.","6oo3au":"The hut's still standing. Shame, really.","ntxoik":"Chicken legs, skull fence, cabbage smell. Like coming home. Only worse.","w9ieu6":"Hello, hut. Please don't run off.","r2es0f":"Back inside. Don't touch anything, Petya. Especially not the stuff that winks.","zu2bdx":"Still smells of socks and magic.","15ac5oq":"The red light. It's starting to feel familiar. Worrying.","199l75n":"Outside the banya again. My life is a series of bad ideas.","1s93srt":"Back in the banya. I'm practically a regular. That should concern me.","1entxh9":"Steam, bass, Madame. Business as usual.","123ah9u":"The village. Still no electricity. Still no surprise.","1wvforc":"Back again. You can smell Grandpa Grisha from the village gate.","1h32lhs":"The village street. The granny at the garden gate is staring again.","1dunzut":"Chicken muck and sunflowers. A classic.","3km4hg":"The graveyard. The cat's still here. Of course.","qpqy4l":"Back with the dead. Quietest neighbourhood in the whole forest.","11kj9s":"The mill. The door is still nailed shut. From the inside. Still weird.","53ae89":"The waterwheel is turning. I'd have been disappointed otherwise.","1r8g5p1":"The dark path. My favourite place. Not.","1knpfba":"Back again. I assume the birches missed me.","1jm8pch":"The swamp. My socks still haven't dried from last time.","ei4hy0":"Hello, ladies. Just passing through. As always.","1ig2net":"Kuzmich is sitting there as usual. I think he's grown roots.","szosbf":"The lake. Smells of fish and resignation.","1f94k87":"The shore. The boat has still given up. Respect.","1dnwufa":"Back by the water. I'm still not jumping in.","7hol5t":"Under the pier. Still draughty. Still dripping.","1qnio8w":"Back in the dark. At least nobody can see me here.","1min79":"The gnomes. The noses haven't got any smaller since last time.","1i778zk":"Back with the gnomes. I'll keep my head down. Out of respect.","cb7nwm":"The cave. The giggling at the back is still there. Lovely.","1jgxhmh":"Cold, damp, mushrooms. Feels like my old flatshare.","116rge9":"I'm Petya. I think. My legs feel like cold pelmeni.","eiofra":"Somebody pinch me.","1luk4iy":"...Nobody there. Typical.","1a69yct":"It's just a trip. A very, very long trip. Happens. ...To me, anyway.","1hpmfo1":"Good morning, Petya. It's already noon.","6qcnc":"The sun is talking to me. Marvellous. Now the sun as well.","1nw5xqk":"You want to wake up? Ask the old woman in the woods. Baba Yaga knows who sleeps here and why.","6nmjng":"Follow the path, Petya. At the crossroads, go to the witch. I'll light the way. ...Just this once.","de2yz5":"Whoever falls asleep in this forest doesn't wake up easily.","1tip0vh":"Thanks. Very reassuring.","jv1cy9":"Psst. Eat me and you'll see colours that don't even exist.","3x9im4":"I'm already seeing them, mate. All of them.","7418g6":"Psst. You don't belong here. Even a mushroom can smell that.","1dkiywn":"Go to the witch. She knows what's growing in your head.","1j0kztd":"Baba Yaga, mate. Hut on chicken legs. Past the crossroads. Now let me grow in peace.","p6atsb":"No, Petya. You've sampled enough for one day.","lblbg6":"Old birch","7u4q48":"The birch is looking at me.","1dt61wq":"Still looking.","vxjbi3":"Go away, you smell of city.","1692b91":"Gladly. Where to?","1cpw963":"To Baba Yaga. You're her problem, not ours.","pyiwxb":"The whole birchhood is talking about nothing else. A city boy in the forest. Go. To. The. Witch.","1tf6ez":"All right. I'm going.","evpgrx":"And you smell of firewood.","uxe95r":"Hey, crow. Catch.","xu8x0v":"CAW! Are you mad?! I showed you the way, you ungrateful lump!","t74855":"I'm telling Baba Yaga! Caw!","1h7yfug":"Right. The branch is free.","1ld398m":"Caw! What are you gawping at my branch for?","tr8ugk":"Nice branch. Straight. Fishing-rod material.","581k84":"You'll never get it! I'm not moving! Caw!","d446gt":"She won't come down voluntarily. Maybe if I throw something at her.","1qomjbe":"Something to throw... Something round, not too heavy.","1apmv0g":"Wasn't there an apple tree at the crossroads?","1v26eng":"Caw! Still here? To the WITCH, sleepyhead! Down the path, at the fork to the hut! Caw!","18lb6tw":"Caw! Another one who won't wake up!","18o44i9":"Another one? How many are there?","15n2eqv":"Ask Baba Yaga. Her hut is deeper in the woods. Caw!","15y1hv9":"The one with the house on chicken legs?","ux85vx":"Caw! And she does nothing for free.","1sapx5":"Tree stump","9e0w4p":"A tree stump. Someone chopped wood here once.","16ttj6b":"Or the birches ate him.","slqs2y":"I'd rather not sit on it. Who knows if it talks too.","1fimcej":"Joint stub","gl13zb":"There it is. What's left of my joint. The culprit.","y95pis":"I'm taking it. As evidence.","8mtttp":"Sign: To the path","1apwzqm":"Sign: To Baba Yaga","1rlm7qz":"Sign: To the swamp","rgfnyo":"Fallen birches","1nxussj":"Firewood for three winters. Vova would flog it.","12ks9m9":"I can't get over it or under it. I need a saw.","1k9ikor":"The sign points to the swamp. Unfortunately there are a few tonnes of birch in between.","1boer6b":"Sign: To the crossroads","1t34irb":"Sign: To the birch forest","2xyify":"Fallen birch","1qwb5rh":"A fallen birch. You can step over it if you don't think about it.","gxx9q9":"Beyond it, it smells of swamp. And trouble.","1vtbsyv":"Sign: To the fisherman's hut","oi4gcb":"Sign: To the dark forest","1b9iupx":"Fisherman","zwd829":"Afternoon. Are they biting?","13d6hja":"The fish? No. The women in the swamp, yes.","1pmysdf":"Thirty years I've sat here. Caught: two boots, a bicycle and my first wife. Fixed the bike. Gaffer tape. Not the wife.","1svp8jf":"Do you know how I get out of here?","v7uibj":"Out? In 1987 I popped out for cigarettes. Taped the engine up and – well. Here I am.","eugfvm":"Ask the old crone in the hut on chicken legs. Baba Yaga. Anyone stuck in this forest is stuck because of her.","ydlabr":"Still here? Back to the crossroads and then to the witch, boy.","wnftq5":"And take vodka. Sober, she's unbearable. Same as me.","1ndgxur":"NOT NOW! THE CATFISH! He's dragging me off the pier! The pier's held together with spit!","1f46gu1":"Take your time.","1pwdyws":"What's wriggling in your pocket?","14npone":"Nothing. ...Just a few worms. For later.","1rhbzu5":"(His line hangs under the pier. That's where the worms go.)","14ubinf":"The bottle stays here. Unless the catfish finally bites. Then I couldn't care less about anything.","1h4r9id":"(Couldn't care less. Not even about the bottle. Interesting.)","pi4ngy":"You won't lure him with bread. He wants something alive. And all I've got is bread and gaffer tape.","1btx9q8":"(His line hangs down under the pier. You could hang something on it... Something alive.)","1pne21d":"(Something alive that a fish eats... Worms.)","q3mkse":"(There was a heap of them outside Baba Yaga's hut. They're bound to still be wriggling.)","1ic89ph":"(Something alive that a fish eats. Worms. And worms live where it's muddy.)","1bw25vj":"(Baba Yaga's yard is the muddiest place I know.)","8tblgg":"Mr Kuzmich, could I have your moonshine? It's for the old man.","wujvyn":"My moonshine?! For the arsonist? I'd sooner eat my net. Tape and all.","27ig8j":"I don't take my eyes off that bottle. It's fuel, disinfectant and glue. Only if something bites. And nothing big has bitten since 1987.","cxo5n1":"Except the catfish. Lives under the pier. But he only bites on worms. Fat worms. You won't lure him with my bread.","1atqvw0":"Well, a fishing rod! Made it yourself? Looks like an accident. Needs more tape.","19epagl":"Go on then. Keep the float in the middle, don't let the fish drag it away!","pslr7":"Stick and string, boy. And a roll of gaffer tape. That's all it takes. And patience. Which you haven't got, I know.","19mzdf2":"String? Not mine, it's three bits taped together. But in the village Galya has a washing line. Longer than the lake.","1aqi8dd":"And I'm sure you can find a stick by yourself.","183p77o":"(A straight branch... In the birch forest where I woke up, the crow was sitting on a rather nice one.)","97mfie":"Could you give me a fish? For a cat.","1j2ws7l":"For the priest's cat? That little Satan once nicked my whole catch. He gets nothing from me.","vaedjn":"Catch one yourself. No rod? Build one. Stick, string, gaffer tape – off you go.","nrpx5o":"A stick and a string. That's all a man needs. And hooch – cleans everything.","pfuyau":"And where do I get those?","zygodc":"Sticks grow on trees, boy. And string... don't ask me, I've been sitting here since 1987.","1aep9mg":"(Trees... In the birch forest where I woke up, the crow is perched on a nice straight branch.)","y0sbla":"(And string... There's a long washing line on the village street.)","2b2yld":"You wouldn't happen to have a saw? There are birches blocking the path.","1b3lm76":"A saw? Boy, I'm a fisherman. I've got a net, a rod, gaffer tape and a catfish who hates me.","1tsivxg":"Grisha in the village has tools. Built his house himself. And burned it down himself. A professional.","1gmk5ix":"Your... wife.","1aw8hty":"Threw her back. Too small.","cmyl1v":"What are you doing with the net?","ts4imq":"Mending it. With tape. A catfish bit a hole in it. Size of a tractor.","1ioczoo":"The hole?","1sbbgle":"The catfish, boy. Although... the hole as well.","jq25sz":"Out? Nobody gets out of this forest. In 1987 I only popped out for cigarettes.","wun0hr":"Ask the old crone in the hut on chicken legs. But take vodka. Sober, she's unbearable.","poj5to":"Fisherman's hut","1171wfe":"The fisherman's hut. Smells of smoke, fish and loneliness.","12ifizy":"Locked.","s5nsu2":"There's only vodka in there! And fish! And gaffer tape! And vodka!","ra59cg":"Old boat","11xpy2p":"An upturned boat. More holes than bottom.","13cmikh":"It still floats! Taped it up. Just not upwards.","6ko0dc":"Lake","5xjmmv":"Here we go. Cast... and wait...","154a6z":"Oh. It's pulling. Actually pulling.","w0xu3o":"There are fish in there. I can see them. They can see me.","lg2u8s":"Bare hands won't cut it. Without a rod I'm just the bloke on the shore.","ghzm9s":"The lake is so still it's like it's holding its breath.","1ro82sr":"Something moved down there. Something big. I'm not going swimming.","1u97kpl":"Fishing nets","xttwed":"Fishing nets drying. Or modern art. Hard to say.","1wapv7":"Sign: To the village","1yrjnm4":"Ith thith... oh no, I've got my teeth back. Eat thomething, you're too thin! In my day boyth were thturdy. You're a twig. Baba Yaga doesn't like boneth.","hrdj9n":"Granny, I found your dentures.","c7fis4":"My dentureth! Where were they? A week of porridge becauthe of you!","nyeav1":"Under the priest's cat. In the graveyard.","1w3wjma":"*clack* ...Ah. Much better. Tastes of cat, but never mind. Everything tastes of something at my age.","1akqemv":"You want tar? Here, birch tar. Good against rheumatism, lice and men. Against men especially – tested it myself.","1sgqc7m":"*receives a bottle of birch tar*","191chne":"Boy! You're the new one, aren't you? Help an old woman! Young people jutht walk path nowadayth, and I thurvived the war...","1r3feio":"Depends on what with.","1gd37tw":"My dentureth! I cried tho hard at Vathily'th funeral they flew right out. That'th what you lot do to old women.","163jpth":"And now the prietht'th cat ith thitting on them. In the graveyard. Hithing at everyone. Jutht like hith mathter.","aj8heb":"And what's in it for me?","1kuqlga":"Birch tar! Againtht rheumatithm, lithe and men. And I'll feed you. Looking at you maketh me thad.","1uaxc2x":"(Tar. Don't need it. ...Yet. In a fairytale you need everything eventually.)","18prahp":"Afternoon, Granny. You wouldn't happen to have any tar?","9cb6k":"Tar? I have. Birch tar. But firtht... firtht... do you even thay hello theeth dayth?","2hd2kq":"What happened to your teeth?","1ttqijq":"Gone! I cried tho hard at Vathily'th funeral my dentureth flew right out. You young oneth don't even cry at funeralth.","prmybi":"And now the prietht'th cat ith thitting on them. The mangy beatht! Hitheth at everyone. Like my late huthband.","1bqrrub":"Bring me my dentureth and you get the tar. And thomething to eat. You're tho thin. Where'th your mother looking?","1eyswym":"The cat'th gone? Then my dentureth are free! What are you waiting for? Do I have to thpell everything out?","1979vdk":"The cat won't move? The little bathtard lithtenth to nobody. Only hith thtomach. Like all men.","1kove1i":"He only eatth fith. Frethh fith. Everything elthe he thpitth on my doorthtep. Ungrateful, like children.","pho9q5":"Fith you get from Kuthmich at the lake. But he'th a mither. Don't tell him it'th for the cat or he'll choke on hith own thpite.","1vjcd6a":"My dentureth, boy! Graveyard! The cat! Don't jutht thtand there like a potht!","1dse80i":"The graveyard ith by the church. Down the village threet, then follow your nothe. You do know how to uthe a nothe?","bsbem1":"By the way, I reported Grietha at the village gate. Fire hathard. And? It burned, didn't it! Nobody lithtenth to Granny.","12d7flj":"...What? Oh yeth. Church. Graveyard. Cat. Dentureth. Go on, you thorry onion!","14c69nl":"Grandpa, I've got something for you.","eezf69":"Blimey... Is that Kuzmich's moonshine?! Stinks of tar and misery. Perfect, damn it!","1vhkc2x":"*glug* *glug* ...AAAH. Blimey, that warms you up. Like the fire did, bugger it.","11ilofg":"The ladder's yours. Survived the fire. Like me, damn it all.","uvjjm2":"*receives a ladder*","abluyp":"Grandpa, do you have a ladder? I need to get into Baba Yaga's hut. It's on chicken legs.","p4zj6z":"Got a ladder. There, by the stove. Survived the fire, the stubborn sod.","zxstmk":"But nothing's free, sonny. Bring me a drink. My moonshine's... evaporated, damn it.","1irriq2":"Kuzmich at the lake makes the best. But the tight old git won't share. Sleeps with the bottle, ugh.","1whs2pv":"No moonshine, no ladder. I'm parched, boy. Have been since the fire, blimey.","mvudc9":"Kuzmich at the lake. Got a bottle older than you, whippersnapper.","vvfo1l":"Kuzmich never takes his eyes off that bottle. Unless something huge bites, damn him.","9sipqs":"Then he forgets everything. Wife, kids, bottle. Saw it myself. 1987, blimey.","1oh6qdh":"What happened to your house?","133mlqa":"The samovar. Or the moonshine. Or me. Investigation's ongoing, bugger it.","1dku39q":"Fire brigade came from town. Three days later. Took photos. Useless lot.","tci946":"Can I take anything from here?","2qtavz":"Take whatever didn't burn. So, sod all.","1lmtzja":"The stove, maybe. But leave it, blimey. The stove's the heart of the house.","148n0hp":"Dusya, that snake, reported me. A week before it burned. Ugh.","178snzy":"A witch. The second one in these woods. One's got chicken legs, the other's got secateurs, damn them both.","1hkpvis":"Empty house","18izq36":"An empty house. The curtains are still here, the people aren't.","vv1pic":"Granny's house","1h04aap":"Granny's house. Sunflowers, curtains, fresh paint. The only house here that isn't dying.","6yioln":"Grandpa's burnt-down house","1hpscbn":"Grandpa's house. All that's left is the stove.","1eodb2x":"The stove's what matters! The rest was decoration, blimey.","1hxia0a":"Village shop","9uoais":"\"Shop\". The note says: \"Closed since 1991. Back soon.\"","w5pace":"I don't think they're coming back.","15bmjc2":"Boarded-up house","1fy30ad":"Boarded up. Nobody lives here any more.","zzcons":"Yes he does, Kolya. Just won't open the door. Not since the election, ugh.","1wv3137":"Well","1hmr92n":"A well. Something's glittering down there.","1h0rwse":"...A beer can. Of course.","17xjcmt":"Chapel","9bgeht":"A little chapel with a golden onion dome. The only thing in the village that still shines.","3furen":"Sign: Into the village","n0iza2":"Sign: To the village gate","1otois5":"Sign: To the church","1rnnovo":"Sign: Back to the village","ymx6j2":"Auntie Galya's house","1p0iqw7":"Auntie Galya's house. Says so on the letterbox, anyway.","13xzin":"There's a telly on inside. Loud. Since 1987, probably.","luq37q":"Washing line","1p7kftf":"Laundry. A pair of knickers the size of a sail.","j9oqse":"When Galya puts those on, she can cross the lake.","he6asu":"Wooden church","18gl639":"Locked. A note: \"Priest in town. Back soon.\" Dated 1993.","7a8u3f":"The domes are gilded. The roof leaks. Priorities.","1tk7gt8":"Bell","181oxyd":"A bell in the tower. I can't reach it. Luckily. Otherwise I'd ring it.","tbyusp":"Graves","1hdgync":"\"Fyodor, 1931–2024. Never won.\" Never won what, though?","1c7itq1":"Plastic flowers. They last longer than the people.","bzkrxw":"Cat","10a80xp":"Here, kitty. A fish. Fresh from the lake.","1smolep":"*the cat grabs the fish and vanishes behind the church*","161zj9y":"And there lies... Granny's dentures. Yum.","14rhfzn":"Well, kitty? Fancy hopping down for a sec?","172439t":"Okay. Message received. He's sitting on something. Something shiny.","1aye2tf":"He's not budging. Maybe with food.","1rv2gaz":"What do cats eat? Fish. And who has fish? ...Exactly.","x7f552":"Dentures","d0u1tk":"Can't reach it. The cat's sitting on it, glaring.","1k5mqq1":"Granny's dentures. I'm only touching those with two fingers.","1dzossf":"Apple","g47h09":"An apple. Nice and red. Too good to eat...","1mznegm":"...just right for throwing.","6ey1iw":"Apple tree","ul6hig":"An apple tree in the middle of a birch forest. Someone must have planted it. Or lost it.","cb4al2":"The other apples are too high.","13ya0m3":"Branch","1faght":"A nice straight branch. But the crow is sitting on it.","15gxtux":"Caw! Hands off, that's mine!","1mw9osw":"*jump* ... *jump* ... *JUMP*","rn3hsu":"A stick. Future fishing rod. I'm so productive today it's almost worrying.","1gwftsq":"Sign: To the shore","jhpxrt":"Sign: Under the pier","790kxh":"Sign: Back to the shore","adfy4o":"Boat wreck","1a1pzem":"A half-sunk boat. That's what happens when you DON'T mend it.","wdd7c5":"Pier","1b7k8pj":"The fisherman's pier. You can crawl underneath if you stoop.","tcmv5g":"Kuzmich is sitting right at the end. He hasn't seen me. Good.","vw7ej1":"Fishing line","p7vzm":"The line is thrashing like mad. Up top Kuzmich is swearing. Glorious.","8u44uw":"The worms are wriggling on the hook. Now the catfish just has to bite.","15oqv2z":"I skewer the worms on his hook. One after the other. Sorry, lads.","16tnmou":"And now I hold the line and wait. The catfish has to pull properly for Kuzmich to notice.","16ziuhx":"The fisherman's line. Empty hook.","1fux11a":"If something really big pulled on this, Kuzmich would be busy for a while...","1fqrjz9":"The catfish. Kuzmich said he only bites on worms. Fat worms.","1o3mslp":"Bread won't lure the catfish. I need worms for the hook.","1v58l30":"The ground outside Baba Yaga's hut is so wet and muddy... it must be crawling with worms.","1dwd2tg":"Rubbish","19o3fuv":"An empty bottle, a boot, a tyre. Kuzmich's CV.","qokpmw":"Worms","1lwor7e":"Fat worms. Just the thing for a catfish. And for nobody else.","pz7089":"A heap of earth full of fat worms. Who knows what they'll be good for.","4atwrm":"*dig* *squelch* ...A handful. Into the pocket. Yuck.","1ob24hy":"Hands off my worms, layabout! They're for the bloody soup!","163nu44":"I'm only borrowing them.","g0dz6m":"Moonshine","19c6ckb":"HANDS OFF! That's my moonshine! I drink it, I clean wounds with it, I run the outboard on it! I've got my eye on it, boy!","dxpnuq":"*grab*","1pmdktd":"(fighting) COME HERE! COME HERE, YOU SLIMY BASTARD!","snfdpz":"He hasn't noticed a thing. Thirty years of waiting makes you blind.","102s05o":"Ladder","ycrtty":"Ladder costs moonshine. Not pretty-please, whippersnapper.","5mt6y7":"An old ladder by the stove. Singed, but sturdy.","pwld8l":"Hands off, damn it! That's all I've got left. Apart from the stove.","1whqsjb":"Here. These were in the joint. Gone all blue.","10qocxj":"*sniff* ...*sniff*... HA! Dreamsponge. But which strain, smart-arse? There's a hundred bloody strains.","go3a1h":"Whoever smokes it wakes up in MY fairytale. My bloody turf, layabout. That's why you can't get out.","1ilrj95":"Vova. Of course. Of course it was Vova.","kqtjoa":"For an antidote I need fresh ones. And they only grow in that bloody gnome cave. Fetch!","t2lav1":"But the gnomes won't let anyone into their bloody tunnels for free. Worse than tax inspectors, and I should know.","vhxqs9":"I need to get to the banya. Beyond the Maze Wood. Do you know the way?","12ovs8b":"The BANYA? You, smart-arse? Hee hee hee! Wait...","yx3mt":"*rummages in the stove* ...*cough* ...There! My bloody map. Only slightly singed.","ls6cxg":"It says: left twice, right once, straight on once.","nedj5e":"Don't get lost, layabout. In the Maze Wood the trees eat you. Slowly. I've watched.","jjcz74":"Got everything? Then to the table, smart-arse! Move!","8zog2n":"Primal spore, blessed embers, a real tear. And your bloody filter. Bring the lot and we'll roll you your way out.","g6y2ji":"What are you standing about for, layabout? Nothing to do?","1wp345f":"Yes, I have. I need to get to the swamp. Only there are tonnes of birch in the way.","1qhgb3p":"Bare hands won't do it. I need a saw.","y83gg8":"Who has tools round here? ...Grandpa Grisha in the village. He built his own house once.","1q6a4vn":"You've got my bloody map! Clear off, go and get lost somewhere else!","161zyxm":"(The way is on her map. It's in my pocket. I just need to read it carefully.)","daj8oy":"Flour? With gnomes \"flour\" is never flour, smart-arse. Hee hee! None of my business. Officially.","b2telp":"Flour comes from the miller. Obviously. ...There's a sign in the village pointing to the old mill.","1fgujvv":"To the gnomes with the mushrooms! And don't get fleeced, layabout. Big ears. And bloody noses.","170q7bt":"Gnomes. Where do gnomes live? ...Past the fisherman on the shore the path went on. It smelled of pipe smoke.","13qd5f9":"Fresh blue dreamsponges! From the gnome cave! Chop chop, smart-arse!","15n9tg5":"On the table with it! Take it apart! Paper, filter, weed. I want to see what poisoned you.","i6gal6":"Where's the stub, layabout? You didn't smoke it, did you? Bring it here!","w5ax0c":"Table","1emuthu":"I dismantled a joint here. In front of a witch. A sentence I never wanted to say.","1t17hya":"I put the joint on the table.","1jb564p":"Careful, smart-arse! Filter off first, then unroll, then sort.","1oj014x":"A heavy wooden table. Full of notches and stains. I'm not asking what from.","15kasmz":"Stove","wfgm80":"A Russian stove. Warm. Too warm. And big enough for a Petya.","1ltel4e":"It's for pirozhki! ...Mostly. None of your business.","18yargy":"Something's bubbling in the pot. Smells of mushrooms and socks.","19pudww":"Shelf","9c7t2u":"Jars of herbs, eyes and something that's waving at me.","k7smzl":"And two skulls. Hopefully not city kids.","nqu4u6":"Broom","sessmi":"Her broom. I think it flies. I'd rather not sit on it.","16qhp3a":"Window (out)","qnhsf1":"Sign: To the gnome village","1f8espa":"Sign: To the cave","5l2pa1":"HALT, Lanky! Where d'you think you're going? Nobody gets in without paying the toll. Don't draw heat.","8nm7ti":"The cave's our patch. Trade secret. Very secret. Very... trade. You saw nothing.","1xdc4oa":"Sign: To the exit","lzonvf":"A Lanky! Who sent you? Who you with? Nobody comes to the gnomes for no reason. You a copper?","lnqt7n":"I want to go home.","svzgpv":"Then you're in the wrong place, Lanky. Leg it before you blow our patch.","15xq5v8":"Home? Then you want the witch. Baba Yaga. She dreamed you here, she'll dream you out. Not a word about us, mind. *sniff*","1xws6k":"Baba Yaga! Hut on chicken legs! Past the lake, turn at the crossroads! Right, conversation over, push off, we're working.","2rfzwt":"Three sacks of flour. As ordered.","nfj4wb":"*sniff* ...*SNIIIFF* ...OH yes. Pure. Lovely clean... flour. No heat on it.","1fa12gb":"Tunnel's open, Lanky. The Mushroom Master's waiting at the back. Here, lantern. Signed out to you. Keep your head down.","16axv6f":"I need to see your Mushroom Master. In the tunnel.","z8radx":"The tunnel? Not without the toll. Three sacks of flour. Cash only. I mean flour only.","1icxjqp":"Flour? You bake?","1bcyj3e":"...Yes. We bake. Loads. All day. Pies. All legit. *sniff*","1uludun":"The miller's got the good gear. The cleanest. But he's sitting on it, won't ship.","1722rw9":"Three sacks. From the miller. Before that, no tunnel. Subject closed. *sniff*","1oc4n3v":"The old mill. Behind the village. Miller won't open up, but he hears everything. So mind your mouth. *sniff*","13c4i16":"Ask Snobbel. He knew the miller back in the day. Before he nailed himself in. Quietly, mind.","1m89ufc":"Hello. Are you... a gnome?","ss2xct":"A BIG gnome! Little gnomes live in Germany. In front gardens. With fishing rods. Embarrassing, that's no business model.","ek3kd":"We're the Nosy Folk of the lake. Bigger the nose, higher the rank. I'm foreman. The nose is the main tool of the trade, get it?","11zrlfz":"What are you doing with the pickaxe?","2m2gok":"Digging. In the cave. Three hundred years. Officially.","9hhxzn":"And what are you looking for?","1fgyylq":"Nobody remembers. But stopping now would be rude. And bad for business.","15rgupz":"Don't go too deep, Lanky. It's dark back there. And dark's only the beginning. We don't like witnesses.","163ltsb":"*puff* You want to go home too? Go to the witch, lad. Everyone goes to the witch. Just keep me out of it. *puff*","8mualg":"Baba Yaga. Chicken legs. Crossroads. Not another word, or she'll owe me even more. She's in deep as it is. *puff*","1nu4pxl":"The miller wants a wife? *puff* Forty years now. Every one ran off. Dodgy deal, that.","vkdsx0":"All the pretty ones are at the banya. Past the Maze Wood. You'll never find it. *puff* Only the witch. The witch knows everything.","1qdz3oe":"Flour from the miller? *puff* He doesn't ship for nothing. He wants something. Everybody wants something. That's the market.","1xa37uc":"Knock on his door. Behind the village, the old mill. Talks through the door. Always through the door. Careful man. As you should be.","lj86z9":"*puff* ...Another Lanky. Had one last week. Asked the way home. Suspicious type.","9fhp7j":"And?","dpvu9d":"We laughed. For ages. Then he disappeared. *puff* Joking. Probably.","evkt7":"Your nose is... impressive.","199qzx":"Thanks. Had it since 1612. Once smelled a bear before it was born. I'd smell a raid too.","1eert57":"Baba Yaga? She owes me three pounds of mushrooms. Don't give her my regards. Forget we ever talked. *puff*","rhnph7":"Gnome hut","jltd95":"Round door, round window, round residents.","1vkm2r5":"Someone's snoring inside. The walls are shaking.","1k2p29t":"Giant cabbage","8m8k72":"Cabbage. The size of a pram.","bey2xe":"Hands off! That's Snobbel's pension! That's stock!","q6emtz":"Cave entrance","110aetu":"A cave entrance with torches. A cold wind blows out. And muttering.","1pls0lf":"Dark tunnel","ejjaea":"*into the tunnel with the lantern* ...Hello? Mushroom Master?","neta2m":"Shh! Not so loud, the mushrooms are sleeping. And the walls have ears. Let's see...","mb8k1j":"*sniff* ...Dreamsponge. Premium strain. Dried by nymph hands in the moonlight. Expensive gear. Very expensive.","u6uy5r":"Fresh ones only here. Front left, the blue ones. Take a few to the witch, she knows what to do with them. And who to shift them to.","1h8yb2z":"Now out. You're disturbing the mushrooms. And me.","bzpc84":"*from the dark* Primal spore, blessed embers, real tear! And keep it down, you'll bring the heat!","1u8tlls":"The tunnel goes deeper. Pitch black. I'm not going in there without light.","jme96r":"Something giggled back there. No. No, thank you.","4rt9dy":"Crystals","ifiu1y":"Purple crystals. They hum quietly.","g584hd":"If you put your ear to them you can hear... Radio Moscow?","4kez1y":"Glowing mushrooms","1569dlc":"Glowing mushrooms. Hopefully not related to the ones in the joint.","t0vb7x":"Underground lake","hc5zen":"An underground lake. Something white and eyeless is swimming in it.","zmcuhf":"It's waving. I'm not waving back.","n5ohm7":"Sign: To the old mill","162v8vn":"Old mill","z109ed":"*knock knock* I've got something for you. A voucher. For the banya. An evening with a private dance.","sm66x6":"...A WHAT?! *planks crack* *nails fly*","z53odt":"*door opens a crack* Give it here! ...Oh. Oh yes. I need to shave. Everywhere.","4hcq72":"Here, three sacks. The \"flour\". Don't ask what's in it. I won't ask what happens at the banya.","wgcz6n":"*knock knock* Hello? I need some flour.","t5m3mk":"Flour? I've got it. The special kind. The gnomes go wild for it.","1ijh9vn":"But nothing's free. I want something else. A woman. A beautiful bride.","1lple9z":"Forty years I've been sitting here alone. With six toes. No woman comes of her own free will.","qry61l":"At the banya, beyond the Maze Wood, they say the prettiest ones are there. But nobody finds their way through the Maze Wood. Only the witch knows the way.","fc4103":"Madame wants a new girl? Then bring her one! And then for me... you know.","1wybhxe":"There are plenty of women sitting around in the swamp. So they say. I haven't been outside since 1985.","1oovd2o":"Bring me something from the banya! A bride... or at least a dance.","e844tl":"The banya is beyond the Maze Wood. Everyone gets lost there. Only the witch knows the way.","yodprj":"The witch on the chicken legs has a map somewhere. She never gave it to me. Nobody ever gives me anything.","d49rur":"The door's shut. Boarded up. From the inside.","bdtsu4":"From the inside. Who boards up a door from the inside? ...I don't want to know.","e74n38":"Something's creaking inside. Like footsteps. Or millstones. Hopefully millstones.","1u2txkj":"Waterwheel","rcxx94":"A waterwheel. Round and round it goes. For a hundred years, probably.","shmeg":"If I stare at it long enough, I'll get high again. Better not.","13boedc":"Water chute","188l9lt":"A wooden chute carries water from the stream to the wheel. Clever. For 1820.","20p1ph":"Mill pond","1s1f5vu":"The water foams at the bottom of the wheel. Something's glittering between the stones.","775u8o":"...A bottle cap. This world has a litter problem.","7ug9l0":"Millstones","177grlt":"Old millstones. Heavy as Gran's cake.","c6ndf9":"Flour sacks","1m4zld3":"Flour sacks. One has burst. Someone was here. Recently.","1lcjuzf":"Footprints in the flour. Barefoot. With... six toes.","16pv74i":"Old cart","agvoup":"A cart with one wheel. The other one must have run off too.","88cwjt":"Sign: Into the Maze Wood","4f71ly":"The Maze Wood. The name alone. I'm not just strolling in there.","1fg8jpi":"I get lost in supermarkets. First I'll find out who knows the way.","1eukm6n":"The old woman in the hut on chicken legs looks like she'd know that kind of thing. Baba Yaga first.","8vslw0":"Nope. Go in without a plan, come out as mushroom fertiliser. Baba Yaga first.","1cz9qfs":"*peers into the woods* ...The woods peer back. No thanks. Ask Baba Yaga first.","1ltqyu":"Sign: Back to the mill","gtj83j":"Path left","1hn82g5":"Path right","qk7da3":"Path straight on","k8p2ej":"Sign: Shortcut to the mill","1qlbnbv":"Exit","1ur3y3p":"Banya door","v0wgpr":"Banya","6u80li":"A log cabin with pink windows. Music thumping inside. My heart thumping outside.","qp8org":"Steam is coming out of the chimney. Or perfume. Or both.","n2n2j0":"Dark forest","oybv6l":"Eyes are glowing in there. Yellow ones. Lots.","sityx3":"I'll stay in the light, thanks.","1rsycb7":"No path, no trail. Just trees and blackness. I'm not going in there.","7ad4ef":"Nastya's here! A sensation! She dances, she flirts, she drinks the guests under the table. The till can feel it already. Perfect!","azawhf":"Here, sweetie. A voucher: an evening at the banya with a private dance. On the house. You scratch my back – that's how business works.","1rb2hn":"It's not for me. I know a miller...","137j2sc":"I don't care who comes. As long as he pays for the drinks. And keeps his mouth shut.","k1yr2q":"Nastya is the star! Watch the show, sweetie. Applause is free. Nothing else is.","1127uzo":"Well? Found one yet? Remember my list. And don't bring me one that just gurgles. I've got gurglers enough.","1ea35o8":"Pretty, loves to dance, cheeky and wants out. It's all on the list, sweetie. Go ahead and grill the girls in the swamp.","fiymhq":"Listen closely when you ask. The answers give everything away. And tick honestly. I can smell a lie a mile off.","1da95k0":"What is it, sweetie? The swamp isn't going anywhere. My patience might.","lydx8f":"The swamp isn't. But neither are the birches in front of it. I need a saw. ...Anyone who's built a house must have one.","1hnjlq8":"Good evening, Madame. A miller sent me. He'd like a... bride.","1qdkapg":"A bride? Here? Sweetie, this is a dance hall, not a registry office.","1ns9n6w":"But fine. We can help each other. My dancers keep running off. The last one eloped with a gnome. A gnome, sweetie.","1qecic9":"Bring me a new one. From the swamp, plenty sitting there bored. But not just anyone. Here's my list. No funny business.","150cjo7":"If she fits, you get a voucher. For your miller. Or for you. I don't ask, you don't tell.","1oyvuey":"Bar","1nn7hm4":"A kvass, please.","n106ii":"Kvass? Here? Sweetie, we have vodka or vodka.","1x7gm66":"...Vodka, then.","vbavdu":"*knocks it back* ...URGH. That's not vodka, that's drain cleaner.","1ahrtfj":"Another? On your tab?","29tmxo":"I'm already seeing double. Two Madames. That's too much Madame.","p4lor8":"Sweetie, there's never too much of me. Ask the fire brigade. They come every Friday. No fire.","1yhf62":"Tips go in the cleavage, complaints go in the swamp.","rbkz98":"No thanks. I still have to get through a Maze Wood.","w4sjog":"Stage","1rcngzv":"No show today. The dancers have... gone out. For good.","12ldiul":"Nastya (on stage)","1spvm9e":"I'll go a bit closer. Just to... study the technique.","g2fgj7":"Again, gorgeous? Round two costs extra. And you haven't even got a tip on you, poor thing.","yz6722":"*spins round the pole* Well, Petya darling? Pick your jaw up, you've drooled all over my stage. Cleaning's extra.","1p5gfe5":"Just looking, gorgeous, or are you ready for more? More costs money.","42f0bt":"I... er... Madame says there are private dances here?","27nrkk":"For the man who pulled me out of the mud? Fine, just this once, on the house. Come to the lounge, hero.","6nkwmh":"Sign: Back to the bar","6rfi9v":"Sign: Back to the club","1p9fumr":"Sign: To the forest path","s94la4":"Baba Yaga's hut","yo8k84":"Crooked, old, and I swear it's breathing. The hut is breathing.","8hcnt9":"The chimney smells of cabbage. And of... something that is not cabbage.","8lyux9":"Door","rhahpt":"Hello? Mrs Yaga? May I come in?","8yaqy7":"Nobody comes in through the door, smart-arse! The bloody door is decorative!","wwbwx8":"Whoever wants something from me comes through the window. If they can get up there. Hee hee hee!","1xte6gn":"The window is three metres up. And the hut is on chicken legs.","1hpuj2i":"I need a ladder.","iveyg5":"Hello? I just wanted to ask how you wake up from here.","2e68hx":"Knock first, then talk! And wipe your bloody feet, layabout!","1x2529z":"*knock knock*","1dak8zx":"Not now! The stove's hot. Come back later, smart-arse.","2adjrl":"Chicken legs","5roitu":"The legs are twitching. Like a chicken having a dream.","pnveji":"I'm not touching those. They definitely kick.","wcafvm":"Skull fence","13898bq":"A fence made of skulls. And the eyes are glowing.","1fsc1wo":"Is that decoration or a warning?","1g0xzt7":"...Both. Definitely both.","1dt5uxc":"Grandpa Grisha wants booze for the ladder. Naturally. Nothing here is free.","h2phw3":"Who's got booze around here? ...The fisherman at the lake looked like he had some. And like he needed some.","1rbvner":"Somebody in this forest must be distilling. Judging by how everyone looks.","1xjxm95":"I'll have to wander round and look.","zdw4c3":"Hmm. Without a ladder I'm stuck.","n2s1l5":"A ladder... Hang on. I've seen one somewhere.","p75jcd":"In the village. By the burnt-down house, next to the stove. I should ask in the village.","y3j0kq":"A ladder. Have I seen one anywhere? ...Nope. I'll have to look.","l7vfry":"Ladders are where people live. And behind the hut there's a path to a village.","qpvblt":"Better not. Or I'll wake up in an even worse fairytale.","1tn9btq":"Saw","aha20":"Grandpa's saw, sharpened by the smith.","kjufjz":"A red apple. Sits nicely in the hand. Throwing weight: perfect.","ssn1v9":"Stick","1p1361o":"A straight branch. This could become something.","j1g6pq":"String","1wmhh32":"String from a broken fishing net.","em664q":"Fishing rod","1ayffbf":"Home-made. Stick, string, safety pin. Bound to hold.","15ugn1g":"Blue mushrooms","q9x1yw":"Nine blue-tinged mushroom bits from the joint. Dreamsponge?","1of46b2":"Singed map","fdk81t":"Baba Yaga's route map: \"left twice, right once, straight on once\".","1pzzsgo":"Madame's list","194njmd":"Wanted: pretty, loves to dance, cheeky, wants out. No gurglers.","pc91kh":"Voucher","utv38c":"\"An evening at the banya with a private dance\". On the house.","n4hohl":"Doesn't smell like flour. Smells like trouble.","1h86kn4":"Lantern","8xyfn0":"A gnome lantern. Burns with something green.","1ud0i3e":"A handful of fat worms from Baba Yaga's yard. They're wriggling in my pocket.","1xsi80k":"Kuzmich's moonshine. The smell alone could blind you.","cecvi9":"Grandpa's ladder. Singed, but sturdy.","j5a6k2":"Fish","as5ymc":"A small fish. Looks at you funny.","57tphw":"Granny's dentures","1sioavw":"A set of dentures. Smells of cat and graveyard.","1e4aa3w":"Birch tar","1qfuk67":"Smells of campfire and Granny's rheumatism.","19lqhnz":"Hang on... I know that tree. And that one. And that one too.","119mvv2":"Brilliant. Lost. Back, before the trees eat me.","76x7d":"Trees. More trees.","1m7f594":"Was that a giggle?","1e3yy4t":"It smells of perfume here... and sauna.","14038od":"Right. Ladder against the window... hold still, dear chicken legs... no wobbling...","1q5xajr":"*climb* *climb* *creak*","1t3dfjb":"The ladder stays at the window. In case I need a quick getaway. Which is likely.","1dz95oy":"Well, city boy? Looking's free. Touching costs. A lot.","1gbruih":"I'm... not gawping. I'm... getting my bearings.","pmgcd0":"Sure. And I'm just here for a bath, gorgeous.","53whbw":"Know the worst part of drowning? The hair. A hundred years of wet hair and not one useless bloke brings a towel.","ukueg":"The frogs are the only men who hop after me. And even they've got more nerve than you, gorgeous. Tee-hee.","cvqhza":"Come closer, Petya. The last one who looked at me like that is lying underneath me now. Didn't complain. Didn't move at all, actually. Tee-hee.","h7p4de":"I was the most expensive woman in the whole province. Now I'm free and nobody dares. Typical men. Not like Fyokla – nobody'd take her for free.","1k73y76":"Maybe it's the mud.","1al42lg":"Mud is an exfoliant, you peasant. Tee-hee!","p4l4hp":"His wife drowned me. With both hands. I smiled right to the end. Out of spite.","1fx6jwn":"Why are you telling me this?","49dumh":"So you know what I can do with hands. The girls can confirm.","or6ht5":"Matron Ustinya","uqenji":"In my brothel I wouldn't have let you scrub the stairs, sonny. But down here you take whatever the swamp washes up. It washed up my girls, too.","1ksutep":"My own girls sank me here. Ungrateful lot. Hear that, you lot?! Ungrateful!","1r8mz7r":"The house by the river still belongs to me. You'll get the key if you do me a favour. Don't tell Glafira.","r61j4e":"What house?","19oovf":"You'll see, sweetie. Tee-hee.","zb4k6u":"Fyokla","agv63n":"Smell that? That's me. And in two weeks that'll be you, if you keep standing on the bank like an idiot. Tee-hee!","beuvnf":"I used to be the fattest in the village. Now I'm the fattest in the swamp. Career, eh? Just to spite Marfa.","3wrtrs":"Want a feel? It's like jelly. With worms in. Tee-hee-hee!","1dbcc5f":"I'll... pass.","11p8u0a":"Coward. The eels have fewer hang-ups. Girls, he's gone red!","5vvxrx":"Glafira","fh52pt":"The Old One","1n9cw5x":"Blub... sonny... have you seen... my nose? Some pike... ran off... with it. The girls... laughed...","1y0j074":"I was... the first here... The curse... is older... than the witch... And these tarts... all they talk about is men...","gr3sq2":"What curse?","xv5iah":"Blub... later... I'm tired... of all of you...","1qkj3v2":"Here. The leftovers. From Vova.","103m7aj":"Finally someone with manners. ...Granny's herbs. Good stuff. Don't tell Ustinya, she'll nick it.","1t2l6of":"Listen, city boy: whoever wants to wake up here needs Baba Yaga's blessing.","1fct0nf":"And the old witch won't lift a finger unless you bleed for it. Bring her something nice. Tee-hee, if you can find anything.","3y8wl3":"What now? Piss off to the witch.","1t1jp5f":"What are you staring at, you tosser? The one who did this to me looked like you. Only with more guts. And better looking.","5watzy":"Got anything to smoke? No? Then shut your face. Girls, he hasn't even got fags!","1pamvuo":"New game","1rhef4i":"Load game","a7gn8d":"Controls","1532dt6":"Settings","1dwr6jk":"Birch forest","fy2sqz":"Crossroads","1p7farv":"Hut (inside)","1p1ttk1":"By the stage","s3w4eu":"Private lounge","hlq7vw":"Maze Wood","37wyhi":"Outside the banya","1ymb96z":"Village gate","1xmaeuq":"Village street","1qywxil":"Church","1ejb4cd":"Birch barrier","17zq3t6":"Swamp","16ivthu":"Fisherman's hut","1wr4frp":"Shore","argow9":"Under the pier","1r1ohvp":"Gnome village","1ietpue":"Cave","dvyoxg":"Out of the fairytale","wye2c5":"Something's not right. I have to wake up.","15zwdye":"Find someone who knows their way around","i2qsce":"From the birch forest to the crossroads, then follow the sign \"To Baba Yaga\". A witch is bound to know how to get out of here.","1yfhpq6":"Get into Baba Yaga's hut","5b3uzh":"Take the ladder to the hut and click the door or the chicken legs – then it's in through the window.","cfqy57":"The door is just decoration, the only way in is through the window. For that I need a ladder (see \"Up and away\").","5vcqn0":"Find out what's wrong with me","1q590jv":"Baba Yaga needs fresh blue dreamsponges from the gnomes' cave (see \"The mushroom lab\").","196xb1e":"Ask Baba Yaga in her hut. She wants to know what was in my joint (see \"The joint\").","nhvtva":"Roll the way-out joint","1eitvis":"The primal spore","1gfwvum":"In the gnome village take the sign \"To the garden\" on the left, click the mushroom bed there and pick five golden mushrooms.","25e9h2":"Embers that never go out","wq07e8":"Find the priest","1t5hhh3":"There's a note on the church: \"Priest in town\", since 1993. Behind the banya (outside the banya, right, to the back yard) someone's snoring in the hay...","1hce0ud":"Get holy water","jd0l5p":"Father Ignatiy is back at the church (village street → \"To the church\"). Talk to him.","9u0e4g":"Win over the smith","1vxb5h3":"Take the holy water to Fyodor the smith in the smithy.","3p2zpd":"Ask Fyodor the smith in the smithy (village street → \"To the smithy\").","1rjllr2":"A real tear","7dx5e8":"Something that makes anyone cry","d14tfy":"Nastya at the banya never cries. A sharp onion? In the gnome garden (gnome village → \"To the garden\") some grow next to the giant cabbage.","dzovrc":"The onion in the vent","1xh15yj":"The lounge vent leads outside: outside the banya, right into the back yard, click the vent there.","17qfz2r":"Get a private dance","d0ovn6":"The guests are gone. Click the stage in the banya and talk to Nastya – now she has time.","1njcv83":"Catch the tear","1qaumq2":"Just stay seated and keep the vial ready.","jdoj2g":"Everything to Baba Yaga","181mtay":"In Baba Yaga's hut, click the table and roll the way-out joint.","1gvmxuu":"The mushroom lab","rxozhk":"Baba Yaga needs fresh blue dreamsponges from the gnomes' cave. But the gnomes don't let anyone in for free.","6qvwah":"Get into the tunnel","swl4xb":"Go to the gnome village (from the fisherman's hut along the shore) and click the sign \"To the cave\". Grobnik wants something for it.","s3edj8":"Get flour from the miller","f6a5ve":"Take the voucher to the miller: at the old mill, click the mill.","15t6nev":"The gnomes want the miller's \"flour\". From the village gate take the sign \"To the old mill\" and knock on the door there (click the mill).","5ng6bx":"The miller will only hand over the flour for something from the banya.","1bduo9u":"The miller's wish","n42iyv":"Nastya is on her way. Back to the banya to Madame Zinaida – she owes me a voucher for the miller.","14as8ie":"The miller wants a bride from the banya beyond the Maze Wood – or at least a dance.","qgyhwh":"Don't lose the way","193kl8q":"Only Baba Yaga knows the way through the Maze Wood. Talk to her in her hut and ask about the banya.","seuhd5":"Find the banya","lc8xzo":"A new girl for Madame","it8x9b":"Read Madame's list in your pockets. Then in the swamp (behind the birch barrier) click the nymphs, talk to them and find the one who fits the list exactly.","11uxs3q":"Fetch fresh blue mushrooms","9hk6fg":"Big blue dreamsponges grow on the left in the cave. Click and collect.","1n5sdic":"Take the mushrooms to Baba Yaga","1c5lcdk":"Back to Baba Yaga's hut and talk to her.","15t099n":"The blocked path","qbup29":"Fallen birches block the path to the swamp.","1rrlks3":"Find a saw","7wcusu":"Maybe Grandpa Grisha has a saw? He's in the village (behind Baba Yaga's hut) in front of his burnt-out house.","rok6b9":"Get the saw sharpened","1cbqiit":"Grandpa's saw is rusty. Village street → \"To the smithy\", ask Fyodor the smith.","14cei7c":"Prepare Grandpa's house","17ofkjf":"The birches on the swamp path are Grandpa's building timber. First he wants tar – Granny Dusya on the village street has some (see \"Granny's dentures\"). Then take the tar to Grandpa.","127mq9x":"Saw up Grandpa's birches","h91hhm":"Take the sharpened saw to the birch barrier and click the fallen birches. The logs become Grandpa's house.","1qeyf8t":"Grandpa's new house","9fjscr":"The logs are at Grandpa's. Now we build: place logs, peel, tar.","cs5e13":"Go to Grandpa Grisha in the village and talk to him.","j07n5p":"An open tab","6vkozw":"Fyodor the smith sharpened Grandpa's saw on tick. \"I forget nothing, boy.\"","1775ba2":"Sooner or later the smith will want something from me. When he says so, I'll know.","1q96l9k":"Granny has lost her dentures. Without them, no tar.","1kjsdw2":"Find the dentures","115mdm3":"Granny says the priest's cat is sitting on them. So: the graveyard by the church (village street → \"To the church\").","1jq2zl4":"Get rid of the guard","c1v8mr":"Something he can't refuse","1gfxsya":"Take the rod to the fisherman's hut and click the lake. Pull against it when he fights!","1nnk1dc":"A cat wants fish. Ask Kuzmich at the fisherman's hut – if he won't hand any over, fish yourself.","opq91z":"Do it yourself","g88g8d":"A stick","110wd5e":"The branch in the birch forest is free. Click it – Petya jumps for it.","1fb0jic":"Throw the apple at the crow in the birch forest (click the crow), then the branch is free.","1pqz5rl":"There's a straight branch in the birch forest – but the crow is sitting on it. Throw something at it? Apples grow at the crossroads.","vv0gdp":"A string","1hrktf3":"There's a washing line on the village street at Auntie Galya's (right).","3oweox":"Give the cat the fish","ph4gxr":"Take the fish to the graveyard by the church and click the cat.","fih48m":"Return the dentures","wju7w6":"To Granny on the village street.","1unm1yz":"Up and away","10reing":"You can't get into Baba Yaga's through the door – only through the window.","1brp5tt":"Find someone with a ladder","16atjlu":"Behind Baba Yaga's hut is the way to the village. A ladder leans against the stove of the burnt-out ruin – ask Grandpa Grisha in front of it.","104ckz0":"Pay the price","1crmvzm":"Take the moonshine to Grandpa Grisha at the village gate.","1t18wa7":"Get the bottle","1x43fxw":"Kuzmich is fighting the catfish! Now grab the bottle on the pier at the fisherman's hut.","rldmg9":"Kuzmich's bottle stands next to him on the pier at the fisherman's hut. As long as he's watching, no chance.","1jc75hk":"Create a distraction","allpr8":"If the catfish under the pier bites on Kuzmich's line, he'll forget everything else.","11s4fxg":"Bait for something big","qxgj8b":"Collect worms","1y43mj":"The ground outside Baba Yaga's hut is damp – fat worms live there.","1qa5twk":"Hang the worms on Kuzmich's line","ika9uj":"From the shore take the sign \"Under the pier\". Click the fishing line hanging through the planks there.","1k9gn0":"The joint","g7wiiz":"Baba Yaga wants to know what was in it.","au7b2i":"Examine the joint","17ecvs7":"In Baba Yaga's hut, click the table and take the joint apart there.","uf9d3b":"The joint stub lies on the tree stump in the birch forest. Take it and put it on the table in Baba Yaga's hut.","1ite03c":"Show the result","1skph53":"Show Baba Yaga the blue mushroom bits (click her).","1qlm2kn":"Pockets","12dtxef":"Tasks","mgnms6":"Map","1nwh25y":"Conversations","y632fq":"Nobody has said anything yet.","cyvn62":"Click an item to look at it.","17xqbg":"Empty. Like my fridge.","1czt40e":"Collect things by clicking them in the world.","gnh1fk":"You are here","15cycp5":"Visited","1kg0oi4":"Unexplored","1i7ftxu":"Nothing to do here right now","8wcmnq":"Left click","1f04dmj":"Walk, look, use, talk","13i9b77":"Click / Space in dialogue","1pxeod4":"Next line","1imdgxs":"ESC / right click in dialogue","1yixk6y":"Skip conversation","2ejlvz":"Signs & doors (arrow)","1f0ga68":"To another place","1acyih7":"Space (hold)","1vk5syq":"Show everything clickable","b2wjv1":"Hint: What should I do next?","1eni4lt":"Conversation log","bcu2cn":"Voices on/off","uvh6z7":"Fullscreen","1rsuknq":"Menu / close","wep9f2":"Small","onobjm":"Normal","1n0h1du":"Large","1qqvvxm":"Very large","19wxd58":"Slow","ic4bts":"Fast","1p1jabm":"Instant","166425m":"Slot","vdr3ol":"Save game","1k8negi":"Load game","1fv1ng":"Voices","160zj11":"Voice volume","1x9bq05":"Music volume","7850re":"Sound volume","12fd7pc":"Idle chatter","13fqjqz":"Text speed","e48qzf":"Dialogue text size","1hwgamf":"Petya:","4eza4l":"This is how big the text will be in the dialogue bar.","1157rug":"Show the tutorial again","1qzrzkn":"Really? Anything unsaved will be lost.","5wjpaa":"Click again","9a6cnt":"This is how I sound.","12kg76j":"This is how we all sound.","wrs743":"is taken. Click again to overwrite.","htohsd":"Saved to slot","11jk25t":"Can't save (the browser is blocking storage).","islgvr":"This is how loud I am now.","1vka7iu":"I won't get out of here on my own. Who lives in a forest like this by choice? Someone creepy, probably.","1bndvyn":"From the birch forest to the crossroads. There are signs there.","1d9mqmv":"The door is decoration. But a house has more than doors.","10740eb":"At the hut. Somewhere higher up.","nrxzdn":"The witch knows something. She just has to feel like saying it.","1416w83":"In Baba Yaga's hut.","1q02i9":"Golden spores. Who grows mushrooms round here, and seriously?","yrzw5j":"In the gnomes' garden.","yji63c":"A priest who's been \"in town\" since 1993. Maybe he never got very far. Priests like vodka...","1n34h59":"Behind the banya.","14gqht1":"The priest is back. Priests have holy water. Usually.","1ap62nj":"At the church.","kykhbk":"Embers that never go out. Who here has a fire that never goes out?","c0n3ng":"At the smithy.","nzyvmp":"What makes everyone cry? Apart from my life, I mean.","cgz5pr":"Vegetables grow in the gnomes' garden.","1mbvy5p":"The onion has to go where Nastya sits. Without her noticing.","1wvutrx":"Now Nastya just has to have time for me.","1477yje":"In the banya, by the stage.","12bszii":"Stay seated. Vial ready. Don't breathe.","q27nq1":"In the lounge.","amog0b":"Got everything. Only the witch and her table are missing.","1pjpcum":"The gnomes don't let anyone in for free. What do they want?","sa0mth":"At the gnomes', by the sign to the cave.","1oinuxp":"The gnomes want \"flour\". Who has flour round here? Apart from Granny.","1va60qd":"At the old mill.","1ih02on":"The miller wants something from the banya. Who'd know about that?","1aenqcu":"In the banya, with Madame.","iwkkgt":"Nobody finds their way through the Maze Wood alone. Who knows their way around everywhere?","1q55sho":"At Baba Yaga's.","6zsa2j":"The map. Read carefully. And count along.","1a5fjfs":"The Maze Wood starts at the old mill.","1o4gkny":"Madame has a list. Somewhere there are women who want out. Out of something wet.","1n8oamh":"In the swamp, behind the birch barrier.","kat1sp":"Blue mushrooms like in the joint. They don't grow in the sun.","omsgzr":"In the gnomes' cave.","v0m5qj":"The witch wanted fresh mushrooms. Now she's got some. Almost.","1xl2jtn":"Birches gone means: saw needed. Who here has built something themselves?","drncc7":"In the village, at Grandpa Grisha's.","1av74aw":"Rusted to the bone. Who sharpens tools round here? Someone with a fire and an anvil.","1levzvw":"Grandpa wants something for his house first before I touch his birches.","lb9kaz":"On the village street, at Granny Dusya's.","1lftkld":"Grandpa agrees. So: sawing.","y0rg8v":"At the birch barrier.","1acowy":"The logs are at Grandpa's. Now he wants to build.","4mcpag":"In the village, at Grandpa's.","1cctjpm":"Granny says the priest's cat is sitting on them. Where do priests' cats sit?","1emlvq2":"In the graveyard by the church.","y4az96":"A cat. What do cats like? Apart from trouble.","4ojleg":"At the fisherman's hut.","1eubcfc":"If nobody gives me a fish, I'll catch one myself. All I need is a rod.","1d1hzok":"Stick plus string.","rkeg7d":"A nice straight branch. I've seen one somewhere.","1qnwihw":"In the birch forest, where I woke up.","wcuama":"Something long, thin and strong. Must be hanging around somewhere.","1jkuy8n":"On the village street.","1o1l5y9":"Fish is here. Cat is waiting.","mumwbj":"Granny is waiting. With an empty mouth.","1fea2rw":"I need something to climb up. Who has one of those lying around?","obhet3":"In the village behind Baba Yaga's hut.","vz0xn6":"Grandpa wants a drink. Something strong.","141mkpn":"Kuzmich is guarding his bottle. As long as he's watching, it's no good.","1eggd5y":"What distracts an angler? A really big catch.","fdjrs5":"Under the pier.","oa0nrp":"Fish want something alive. And worms live where it's muddy.","z80eot":"Outside Baba Yaga's hut.","1u1kizy":"Kuzmich's line hangs through the planks. You could reach it from below.","1vc8s9a":"What was actually in that joint?","1i6c2w1":"The witch wanted to know what was in it.","vt5zyb":"Where do I have to go?","4wkguy":"Show solution","1u9r166":"Hint","1pc6uov":"Show","1yx46s":"Space","xse2tx":"Menu","1wtepwa":"Hm. No idea. Naturally.","b60fmr":"Maybe I'll talk to everyone again. Or have a closer look around. (Space shows everything clickable.)","1u9y4nt":"Let me think...","1ouguo2":"Fine. Thinking. If I must.","oyyg2s":"What was the plan again? Oh, right.","1b3ll3n":"Right now it's about:","17iju69":"Next up:","1bj89zf":"Or I'll deal with this first:","dplmny":"And if I get stuck: ask people. Several times. Somebody always blabs.","1ym367f":"Pocketed:","ehbpqs":"New task:","1m4qraz":"Task done:","y9n0av":"Tasks updated","1qpsxb2":"How to play","krz0uk":"Click in the world","185j6pj":"to make Petya walk. Click on things and people to look at them, take them or talk to them.","1qs2wmf":"Signs and doors","1gai0sc":"lead to new places. The cursor turns into an arrow there.","p37y2o":"Hold Space","1ueo5bp":"to show everything you can click in the scene.","5pehs8":"Stuck?","16jsvkc":"The hint button (H) tells you what's next. All tasks are listed under","1jcnsqs":"Let's go!","12n5l2h":"Continue","1lw6a5o":"Fishing","4c4ksb":"*just yanks with all his might* ...Oh. A fish. Must have taken pity on me.","z0zgdx":"The catfish","15dwk9k":"*just holds the line and waits*","9wucc9":"Take apart the joint","1b0ox3u":"*picks everything apart very slowly* ...Right. Nine pieces. All of them blue.","1sbk7mt":"Next time you can skip \"","1gjd47c":"\".","p94er5":"Not quite working? No problem – you can skip the minigame too.","owc3r8":"Try again","opgpm2":"Skip","15slwie":"Hmm. None of them look like Madame's list. Too old, too wet or too dead.","1d0a7yy":"Maybe different ones will be sitting here next time. Pop out and come back. They must take turns.","17ni6id":"If I stare long enough, the net looks like my CV. Lots of holes, caught nothing.","1ek8ca1":"There's still a cactus on the windowsill. The only one who stuck it out.","oz0x77":"The window smells of cabbage soup. And of reproach.","1mmztjv":"A house without a house. Just a stove. There's something honest about it.","1h3k3qb":"In the shop window there's a tin of sprats from 1991. Bound to still be good. Bound to.","zrxcz1":"Through a crack you can see a telly. It's on. With no electricity. I'm not asking.","f0egzg":"I could throw something in and make a wish. But all I've got is dirt on my fingers. And no wishes a well can grant.","igwo2j":"The dome shines like someone polishes it. Every day. Out of spite.","loh261":"Someone inside just yelled \"GOAL!\". Probably been doing it since 1987.","1k3eynf":"The socks on the line are drier than mine. I'm not jealous, though. ...I am.","1prvigw":"If I could ring it now, I would. Just to see who comes out.","1w99d7m":"Quiet here. Nobody wants anything from me. Almost pleasant.","12lprfw":"A monument to everyone who says \"I'll do it tomorrow\". So, to me.","1k6kgup":"I'd tidy up. But then Kuzmich wouldn't know who he is any more.","1v2wht3":"One jar says \"Do not open\". The one next to it says \"Seriously, don't\".","nv5g6g":"They twitch when I walk past. We're agreed: we don't like each other.","120uhc4":"If you tap the cabbage very gently, it sounds like a drum. I'd rather not tap it.","15lg3jf":"Cold air is coming out of the cave. And a smell like my gran's cellar.","1lv1m5":"Now it's playing schlager. Very quietly. I'll move on.","ntpzrh":"They glow in time. As if they're laughing at me.","ve20r4":"The white thing has come closer. I'm pretending I didn't see it.","1gjz7xi":"Rushing, creaking, turning. Like my head after Vova's party.","16nc551":"A leaf is sailing down the chute. It has more direction in life than I do.","o6144q":"A frog is looking at me. I look back. It's a draw.","1lti0qc":"One of them is cracked. Like my back after the banya.","1lltruf":"A sack says \"FLOUR\". With three exclamation marks. Very convincing.","dl7j6y":"Won't get far on one wheel. I know the feeling.","yurvba":"A smithy yard. Thatched roof, well, woodpile, a carved horse on the gable.","1hf97jf":"The forge is still glowing. No sign of the smith. Probably getting beer. I would.","h01pe5":"To the village street","ru84yx":"Smithy","1u1s7ma":"A smithy made of thick logs. Open, warm, and it smells of iron.","1b04ad0":"If anyone can get something fixed round here, it's the smith. If he were ever in.","12y0fxt":"There's a carved horse on the gable. It's supposed to bring luck.","swg17h":"So far only bad luck has brought me anything. But at least it was free.","5xo35d":"Forge","1eajll5":"The coals are still glowing. The smith can't be far.","cf04hq":"I'll just warm my hands. ...Glorious. The only thing in this fairytale that doesn't want to bite me.","16xrxjm":"Anvil","12b2xv7":"An anvil. Heavy, black, honest.","1eax3ow":"Nobody's nicking that. I've tried. Mentally.","osj910":"Horseshoe","3fyqc":"A horseshoe over the door. Open end up, so the luck doesn't fall out.","hpq9t2":"Mine fell out ages ago.","if6coi":"Haystack","1l3jbtp":"A haystack. Smells of summer and mice.","1eu9nrf":"If I lie down in there now, I won't get up until next year.","104to2e":"Barrel","nhpew9":"A barrel. There's water in it. Unfortunately.","cio4rj":"Well","1krpc48":"A well with its own roof. It's got more roof than I have.","1rmorv3":"*calls down* Hello? ...Just an echo. And a frog looking annoyed.","fw87wt":"Woodpile","z5oofz":"Neatly stacked. Someone here has their life together.","we01z9":"Not me. But we knew that.","802kei":"Sign: To the village street","wnblnr":"Sign: To the smithy","nv9gpe":"It smells of iron, hay and work here. I like two of those.","o36of5":"The well is gurgling. I'm getting thirsty. For kvass.","y3sp6u":"Someone's hammering somewhere. Or it's my head. Hard to tell.","n51prr":"The horse on the gable looks like it knows something.","tz8brw":"The smithy yard. The forge is still glowing.","14qgjx":"Back at the smith's. Fyodor is hammering. Fyodor is always hammering.","4wo6ie":"A few sparks fly up. So do I. Backwards.","buqgf3":"The frog is still here. We're practically colleagues now.","1k05dg6":"Smithy yard","1n8bqwi":"Object","2bot0f":"Father Ignatiy","wvun74":"Fyodor the Smith","10dye6o":"Paper filter","174dctg":"The filter from the old joint. Been through everything. Like me.","1ln0rri":"Primal spore","1cbf2kt":"Golden spores from the gnomes' mushroom bed. They glitter. Smell of cellar and future.","1nq5w5r":"Empty vial","11umkez":"From Baba Yaga. For a real tear. Dropping it is forbidden.","m8ajt7":"Nymph's tear","169ctn":"A real tear from Nastya. Thanks to a gnome onion. I am not a good person.","1bg7zaw":"Gnome onion","p45217":"The sharpest one from Snobbel's bed. My eyes water through the pocket.","pv82ol":"Holy water","1mmsvbg":"From Father Ignatiy. Topped up with vodka \"for shelf life\".","gokh3e":"Embers in a tin","2sotv7":"Blessed embers from Fyodor's forge. They never go out. Not even in the swamp.","bigh3w":"Way-out joint","1lhpdw5":"My way home. Hopefully.","1p91qn4":"Nastya is freshening up. I've got maybe a minute.","16oeur8":"(And that vent up there blows straight onto the sofa...)","1xldkb5":"GONE!","17h9qud":"Excuse me... You wouldn't happen to be the priest from the village?","117jx9q":"*hic* Father Ignatiy. At your service. Only here briefly. For a beer. Beer is also a gift from God.","1k3fyzj":"There's a note on your church. \"Back in five minutes.\" From 1993.","1lj6fmc":"To be honest, I'm not too sure how I got here either.","19rkiga":"Lord in heaven. The bells! The cat! My congregation! ...Well, it's all for the best. Probably.","1m07jq2":"Your congregation consists of one granny and one cat. Both furious.","10chrn2":"I must go back. But through the Maze Wood? Can't find it sober. And the last time I was sober was 1993. The Lord forgives.","rx9p3g":"Left, left, right, straight on. Only backwards. So: straight on, right, left, left.","4t5chz":"God bless you, my son. See you at the church. Just one for the road. It'd be a sin not to.","19y1265":"My son! The church still stands. So does the cat. He's got fat. The Lord's will.","km0mym":"I need embers from a blessed forge. Only the smith doesn't have a blessed forge.","1htzpju":"Fyodor? I've owed him the blessing of his forge since 1993. He reminded me every year. Loudly. Humility isn't his virtue.","13bmeqd":"Here: holy water. The real thing. I only added a drop of vodka. For shelf life. The Lord won't mind – He values durability too.","zjylps":"Of course.","vhnk7o":"Take it to him. Tell him: that makes us square. With God and with him.","5b1yff":"Give Fyodor my regards. And tell him: square means square. Forgiveness, my son. Especially of debts. Mine.","v0xgpj":"The cat sits on the altar now. I let him. He's been in the congregation longer than me. And donates more.","1wdrcgo":"May the Lord guide you home. And if not, there's vodka at the banya. He moves in mysterious ways.","9s4lgc":"Mind the tin. And your fingers. Debts? Chalk at the ready.","juwr33":"Regards from Father Ignatiy. Holy water. He says: square.","1ompkd3":"*tips it into the forge* *HISSSS*","if0oyk":"...Smells of vodka.","1s0q74j":"For shelf life, he says.","b0nqys":"Then it's real. Here. Embers. In a tin. Won't go out. Not in the swamp either.","5ukcwf":"*takes the tin* Hot. Naturally.","mydlt":"*wipes a chalk mark off the wall with his sleeve* Square. Chalk stays ready.","v9jfb7":"I need embers. Embers that never go out.","nkm2uc":"My forge? Burns unblessed. Thirty years. Priest was meant to. 1993. Then: \"into town\".","1tn77t0":"Owes me since. No blessing, no embers. That's it.","1la21ql":"And if I bring you the blessing?","5ack63":"Then you get embers. The best. Whole fairytale.","2qktxq":"What you gawping at? Never seen a smith?","4x1lmc":"I have. On telly. They were smaller.","o90tj3":"Horseshoes. Nails. Scythes. No miracles. Miracles – witch.","1924g0c":"I hit iron. Not people. Mostly.","14z0858":"Can't pay – on the wall. In chalk. Chalk at the ready.","102g00w":"Mushroom bed","1nc5a2m":"The bed has given me enough. The mushrooms look offended.","yog525":"A mushroom bed. The mushrooms are looking at me. I'd rather look away.","tcznya":"Hands off, Lanky! That's gnome gold. It's on the books.","1u3mu8v":"The primal spore? Bulb sent you? *sigh* Clients everywhere.","1twfo3y":"It's the golden ones you want. Pop up and vanish faster than a market stall in a raid.","sf2ep":"Five golden ones and you've got enough spores. But pick a wrong one and the bed gets upset. An upset bed draws heat.","1mnkcro":"A mushroom reaction test. My favourite sport. Right after lying down.","9adcpp":"Vent","uwur4d":"There's an onion in there now. Respect to the vent.","hnft5l":"The vent blows straight onto the sofa. But in here Nastya sees everything.","1c7ec5b":"(It'd be less obvious from outside. Behind the banya.)","90f06r":"A vent. Blows warm air straight onto the sofa. Who builds something like that?","120elm0":"Granny, you wouldn't happen to have an onion? A really sharp one?","1b4uprg":"My onions are all in the soup, boy. Everything goes in the soup, my whole life. But the gnomes grow some. So sharp the cabbage next to them weeps.","18t2zou":"Onionth? All in the thoup. The gnomeths have thome. Thharp onth. Like me when I wath young.","1op9ghz":"Nastya... really weird question. Could you cry? Just one tear?","1bafqpe":"Cry? Darling, I spent three hundred years lying in a swamp. No tears left. Only mud. And the mud costs extra.","11qh08a":"(A real tear from someone who never cries. Marvellous.)","1hm4wmc":"(Something that makes everyone cry... Onions. The gnomes grow vegetables.)","6n2mq1":"Private dance? Ask Madame, gorgeous. She runs the till. And the bookings.","zftx2y":"Madame, I'd like another private dance. With Nastya.","1p416ca":"Again? Sweetie, you're getting hooked. I like that.","1409zi7":"Oh, all right. For my best recruiter. Lounge is free. You owe me one, mind.","191fxwf":"Right, gorgeous. I'm here. Hands on the sofa – and behave.","1qsw556":"(Don't breathe. The vent's already working.)","42l8zp":"(Hang on. If I walk into the lounge with an onion in my hand, Nastya will notice straight away.)","120srut":"(The lounge vent has to come out somewhere. Behind the banya, maybe?)","175z4mj":"The door is open. It smells of incense inside. And of vodka.","1vc5cmw":"Now it glows blessed. And smells faintly of vodka.","s6oeuw":"Fyodor's forge. The coals are glowing. But somehow... unblessed.","1vox9qc":"This is where I built my way out. A sentence I never wanted to say.","1hjme9a":"Well? Primal spore, blessed embers, a real tear. And the old filter. All of it on the table, layabout.","rtkrs0":"And roll it properly. A wonky joint only takes you to the next bloody fairytale.","1m8indw":"This is where I'll build the way-out joint. As soon as I've got everything.","6sekuh":"Primal spore, blessed embers, real tear. And the filter. I'm not lifting a finger before that, smart-arse.","nt3vax":"Five golden mushrooms. The spores glitter. Smells of cellar and future.","142nk9x":"Done. Now off my bed, Lanky. We've never met.","1ijgdly":"Click the GOLDEN mushrooms before they vanish! Not the brown or red ones.","cl4zc9":"Cancel","15b96rg":"Toadstool! Hands off!","14d4mjm":"That's a perfectly ordinary mushroom.","960ale":"The bed is offended.","16xbd6s":"The mushrooms were faster. Embarrassing. Against mushrooms.","b759vh":"Put the filter at the right-hand end of the paper.","1hny1s9":"Filter first, sonny!","wuwuer":"Primal spore on first!","l6y15a":"Now the tear!","1p2f3my":"Roll it first!","u7w7tt":"Now light it!","1blg7ae":"Primal spore onto the paper","1kbh2ve":"A drop of tear","99zom7":"Embers to the tip","1d25k29":"Later","1fb9kk6":"Now light it: hold the embers to the tip on the left.","5vxtop":"Now sprinkle the primal spore onto the paper.","u003m2":"Add a drop of the tear.","75j74v":"Now roll: drag across the paper from left to right.","1x433s5":"Later? The fairytale won't wait forever, layabout. ...Oh, all right, it will. Got nothing else on.","184iymf":"Roll the way-out joint","15mb7eg":"Done. The most beautiful way-out joint I've ever seen. And I've seen more of them than you've had bloody breakfasts.","1s0hhdx":"Take a drag, smart-arse. And give my regards to the real world.","41lziu":"Well then. To the way out.","3l7nvd":"*cough* ... *COUGH*","6l7jr0":"Sofa. Saturday. My flat.","1gf636a":"I'm... back?","14q9zsa":"Right, listen: I've got something. Brand new. Proper mental, you get me? Granny's herbs, bro!","49i6n7":"Vova.","1wso381":"Eh? What?","52kn4i":"Out.","bh7ybj":"You're having me on – there's these funny little blue mushrooms in it...","1o42k99":"*stares at the mushrooms*","17loldt":"...Marvellous.","x04l6m":"the bloke on the sofa","e9s0xt":"the reason for everything","yqmuoj":"witch, cook, life coach","ithufr":"science","1vplc49":"Grobnik & Grandpa Snobbel","3mprlw":"gnomes, tolls","o69wi":"Kuzmich","11yht1k":"fisherman, moonshiner","1yfvote":"dentures, tar, onion","1ozkaow":"ladder, saw, new house","1r02lfq":"star of the banya, never cries","17lr88o":"in the hay since 1993","1tpg0m0":"got his blessing","gsxn11":"The Crow","66n915":"Caw","1yvqrsd":"The priest's cat","1ovdqwz":"played himself","1fd4kfa":"and the Cursed Birch Forest","al9u09":"The End.","14joj5s":"...or is it?","108ptcu":"Cast","1pjg6lu":"No mushrooms were harmed","4meyi1":"Except nine blue ones. And five golden ones.","1ck87f9":"And one onion.","49l39w":"Thanks for playing!","vj6yuq":"To the title screen","c85bu":"Keep looking around","1psbhbj":"Rusty saw","1ufq88r":"Grandpa's saw. Survived the fire. These days it only cuts faces.","1d2czyd":"Grandpa's saw, sharpened by the smith. On loan. In exchange for an entire house.","1tsx7x2":"Auntie Galya's old washing line. Smells of carbolic soap. Bound to hold a fish.","1q0fw55":"Right. Here goes. *puts the saw to the wood*","bx46xm":"*far, far away* *WHEEEEET* OI! WHERE D'YOU THINK YOU'RE GOING, YOU LITTLE SOD?!","1jl0bsg":"...Grandpa? The village is on the other side of the forest!","6uju4d":"I can hear my saw! It squeaks when it touches someone else's wood, blimey!","1jddwn1":"That's MY timber, damn it! Tar first, then you saw. A deal's a deal!","4vtb7u":"(How does he do that?)","c7pabi":"*from afar* BOY! HANDS OFF MY BIRCHES, BLIMEY!","98nn75":"*from afar* I can see you! ...Ugh, bugger, I can't. But I KNOW!","lwoj":"(No chance. First bring Grandpa the tar. Granny Dusya on the village street has tar.)","4qm2gv":"Grandpa's birches used to lie here. Now he lives in them.","gqx7gf":"*scratch* ... *scratch* ... *squeak*","fjnp1w":"The saw just slides off. It's so rusty it wouldn't even cut butter.","78navy":"That rusty thing's useless. Somebody needs to sharpen it.","19rh365":"(Who sharpens tools round here? Someone with a fire and an anvil...)","17aec4m":"A smith! There's a sign on the village street pointing to the smithy.","1raet4q":"Fallen birches. Tonnes of them. I can't get through.","6awkdz":"Don't need to right now, though. I think.","hqciu0":"Hmm... maybe Grandpa has a saw. He built his own house once.","17scfns":"Grandpa Grisha in the village. Anyone who burns his own house down built it himself first. He's bound to have tools.","rcxehu":"Right. With Grandpa's blessing. *saw* ... *saw* ... *pant* ... *saw*","jmpupt":"Done. The path to the swamp is clear.","kuye1n":"And now... the logs to Grandpa's. All of them. My back already knows.","ou63gf":"Wood scraps","1g5h78i":"*haul* ... *haul* ... *haul* ...","2440l2":"About bloomin' time! The logs are here. Now we build, the old way:","1vjnx4k":"Log on log. Then the bark comes off, or the damn beetles eat the house. And tar in the joints at the end.","1dt9omh":"*Two days later*","oj8z73":"There! A house, damn it! Real birch logs! And the stove was already here.","15lnr5b":"My back has burned down too now.","dq5tiz":"Keep the saw. You've earned it, whippersnapper. Now off to your swamp, the path's clear.","61hzwo":"Click when the log is right above the wall!","1tn49pm":"Peeling: hold the mouse button and drag the drawknife over the logs.","1wonws0":"Perfect fit!","ifx787":"Like a glove!","pkqva":"Grandpa nods.","796yn":"Straight as a ruler. Nearly.","15f9ujp":"Another one!","fp5kzd":"Missed! Again.","182tzlr":"It's rolling away... Again!","1oyq2bp":"Grandpa: \"Gently, boy!\"","weo7qq":"Bark off:","j51g48":"Joints tarred:","mo35of":"Logs:","om7ac7":"Phase 1 of 3 – Place the logs","zefxb4":"Phase 2 of 3 – Peel","1734aoe":"Phase 3 of 3 – Tar the joints","12lhhyk":"Done","1f61wzn":"Tarring: brush the tar into the joints.","13wpy2x":"Finished! A real log cabin.","aptq69":"A break? Ugh. Fine. The logs won't run off. Say when.","1wli8mm":"Build Grandpa's house","rp62a0":"Grandpa! Birch tar. From Dusya. Against rheumatism, lice and men.","ois7u0":"Ha! Tar! Blimey, now the wood won't rot before it's a house.","9oirqt":"*smears the corner by the stove* Right. Spot's ready. Now you may saw my birches. Carefully, damn it.","1nitlzg":"Saw 'em up and haul the logs over. Then we build. And your swamp path's clear too, blimey.","m7vbni":"Grandpa, you wouldn't happen to have a saw? There are birches lying across the swamp path.","15wij5h":"A saw? Got one. Was in the stove. Stove survived the fire, saw too. Sort of, damn it.","fa1az6":"*rummages in the ashes* There. Bit rusty. Rust is just patina, says my brother-in-law, the idiot.","1ipu461":"Hang on, damn it. The birches on the swamp path? The storm laid those down for ME. That's my timber for a new house!","1vn4hok":"And if I saw them up for you? Then my path is clear and you've got your wood.","1lr9r":"Deal! But first we prepare. Without tar the wood rots, ugh.","6bug66":"Dusya on the village street has tar. Tar first, THEN the birches. And heaven help you if you saw before – I can hear my saw two kilometres off, blimey.","dws0af":"*receives a rusty saw*","zb4nyo":"Tar? One moment.","1ws5iq5":"*pulls Granny's birch tar out of his pocket*","1ija8su":"...You walk around with TAR? Damn it, who walks around with tar?","1r3h6q8":"Long story. Involves dentures.","1i2ww31":"*smears the corner by the stove* Well then. A deal's a deal. Saw away as soon as the saw cuts again.","lz08f9":"Grandpa, the saw doesn't cut. It's completely rusted.","1xf597t":"Patina, boy! ...Ugh. Bugger it. Rust.","go8dkq":"Go to Fyodor at the smithy. Down the street. Sharpens anything. Even mothers-in-law, blimey.","103rp7g":"Tar first, then birches. No tar, no house, damn it.","6sojb8":"Dusya's got tar. But she won't give you sod all till she's had a good moan. Listen to her. Grit your teeth.","9737i":"Dusya's moaning about her dentures. For weeks, blimey. Help her, you get the tar.","cbbh5w":"Logs are ready. Sleeves up, whippersnapper!","12bg28a":"Tar's on. Now the birches, damn it! Saw 'em up and bring me the logs.","1bu5u9w":"A house! With a stove! Blimey, the stove was here already, but now it's got a job again.","jk5ih":"This time I'll be careful. No more samovar in bed, ugh.","17bo8ev":"And the moonshine?","rn5f7t":"That stays. No need to go overboard, damn it.","1w8rby8":"If you ever need a roof over your head, boy – knock. Not too hard. Fresh tar, blimey.","w74v0d":"Grandpa's new house. Crooked, but standing. And I built it. Half. A quarter.","1gopimy":"And it smells of tar! Like a proper home, damn it.","1soqkfl":"So this is where the new house goes. The stove is already standing. The rest is lying on the swamp path.","131ep28":"A washing line. Long, thin, strong. Perfect fishing line.","187d367":"*unties the line* ...I'll leave the knickers hanging. Out of respect.","hs9lnq":"*from across the way* Go on, take it, boy! Galya never gave my line back either! God sees everything!","1s6pj1t":"The laundry is lying in the grass now. Galya will be thrilled.","3txw9s":"Good day. Could you sharpen this saw for me? It's Grandpa Grisha's.","g60e7t":"Grisha's? He burned his house with... No. Samovar.","1iolus8":"*turns the saw* Rusty. To the bone. Give.","1kjd4rx":"*grind* ... *spark* ... *grind* ... *ZING*","7k4wqu":"There. Cuts excuses now.","v98v4v":"What do I owe you?","1bpwf4x":"Money?","gcs1af":"No.","1k8ch86":"Then I write it down. Chalk at the ready.","wcw6rn":"Chalk at the... what?","v47g1k":"Chalk at the ready. Chalk in my apron. Always. I don't forget. I need you – you come.","12ketwe":"Holy water. Then square. Till then – chalk at the ready. No embers.","jlx5wl":"Ah. Debtor. The saw. Written down. Chalk at the ready.","1ulzqo5":"Time's come. Forge unblessed. Since 1993. Priest was meant to. Went \"into town\".","1ijdewr":"Bring holy water. Then square. Embers on top.","piy6w9":"Holy water. From a priest who's been in town for thirty years. Sure.","12mymrq":"Saw cuts? Good. You owe. Written down.","15fwgw2":"*pats his apron* Chalk at the ready.","12av5uy":"Behind the banya. Crates, empty bottles, a haystack. And the vent is blowing perfume into the forest.","ljov2d":"Hang on. The haystack is... snoring.","8yelf4":"To the entrance","tugmaw":"Back yard","xpvs9h":"Sign: Back yard","104pnlp":"Sign: To the entrance","yzemij":"Back wall","1cxc0wq":"The back wall of the banya. The bass is thumping through the planks.","1wm39ws":"The wall dances better than I do.","1mfdhyn":"Back door","7927lm":"The back door. Locked. This is where they carry the guests out at night, I reckon.","14pkp0y":"Empty bottles","1yh2h6c":"Crates full of empty vodka bottles. The banya is having a good month.","jf53u0":"Or a bad one. Depends who you ask.","vlndc":"There's still a hollow in the hay. Priest-shaped. Thirty years deep.","1lhki1w":"Lounge vent","1xdy4id":"There's an onion stuck in there. The vent now smells like a vegetable market.","1eheto1":"The lounge vent. Blows straight onto the sofa, Nastya said.","1e5zvfp":"*squeezes the onion through the grille* ...In you go.","13pnp5u":"Now just book a private dance. And don't breathe.","1jm8t1n":"The lounge vent. Warm air, perfume and bass.","1wq3e8s":"(If something really sharp got in here... everyone in there would be bawling.)","1pmw2fj":"A vent. Warm air, perfume and bass. The private lounge must be in there.","1eie6c9":"There's a priest lying in the hay. Behind a strip club. Snoring.","lqyj08":"I'll let him sleep. Anyone who snores like that has earned it.","nvzwjw":"*quietly* Hello? ...","1gpicls":"*Snore*. Okay. He wouldn't wake up if the church collapsed.","lknuhq":"*mumbles in his sleep* ...just one little blue... mushroom... to relax... the Lord forgives... just close my eyes for a sec...","17ki70i":"(A priest dreaming of blue mushrooms. I'd rather not ask.)","uq9txt":"Father? ... FATHER!","xmi44c":"*snore* ... five more minutes... to the glory of God...","1vtbank":"*tickles his nose with a straw*","pztnc":"AAA-CHOO! Who? What? Where am I? Is it the Last Judgement?","1o7ky1":"Behind the banya. In the hay. There's a note on your church: \"Priest in town.\" From 1993.","nq0e84":"The beer... and one of those little blue mushrooms with it. From the old woman in the woods. \"To relax\", she said. One mustn't refuse one's neighbour.","19uo0o3":"Since then everything's been so... sluggish. As if I never properly woke up. Thirty years, you say? Well, I'm rested.","zoyye1":"(Blue mushrooms. Thirty years in the hay. Note to self: eat nothing blue round here. And don't lie down anywhere for long.)","1t5p46z":"God bless you, my son. See you at the church. Donations welcome.","1tox6b5":"Behind the banya","1whh4r0":"The bass is thumping through the wall. The crates are shaking along.","18zkk3d":"Back here it smells of hay, vodka and perfume. In that order.","11e9czp":"Eyes are glowing in the woods again. I'm staying in the light.","t8c865":"Behind the banya. The haystack is still here.","1qg9pyc":"Behind the banya again. It's quieter here. Apart from the bass.","10h9d9o":"Vegetable patch","y8ob6l":"Onions! Next to the giant cabbage there are onions.","17awylv":"*pulls one out* ...AAH. My eyes. Just from pulling it out.","edyftt":"Oi! Hands off Snobbel's veg! Not for sale! ...Yet.","87fkim":"Just one. For a good cause. I want to make a nymph cry.","v51qjw":"...That's the worst good cause I've ever heard. Take it and go. You never saw me.","1mb9di8":"A vegetable patch. Giant cabbage and onions so sharp the air shimmers.","1qmvmi":"From the gnomes' vegetable patch. My eyes water through the pocket.","1kkst2l":"A real tear from Nastya. Thanks to a gnome onion in the vent. I am not a good person.","8a7npw":"Fresh dreamsponges","1baibmp":"Big blue mushrooms from the gnomes' cave. They glow in my pocket. That's bound to be normal.","tmii6c":"There! Big blue mushrooms. Same colour as the bits from the joint.","1moe13k":"They're glowing. In my hand. Marvellous.","u6415v":"Off to Baba Yaga with these.","9cwcg4":"I've got enough. I don't want to explain any more glowing mushrooms in my pocket.","1ruavvr":"*sniff* ... Fresh blue dreamsponges. And your bloody joint was STUFFED with them.","wekd06":"*stomps back and forth* Do you know what that means, layabout?! This isn't a trip. It's a HOUSE MOVE!","1ekkoxk":"That's how deep it goes. Into the bones. Into the dreams of your bloody dreams!","1i6aade":"Is that... bad?","vgnh9c":"BAD?! *very close* Listen here, smart-arse!","1f3bj73":"Without an antidote you will NEVER wake up. Never! Then you live here. With ME. FOREVER! Chopping my bloody firewood!","15eqn9r":"I'll roll you a way-out joint. But I need three bloody things for it:","iwm426":"First: the primal spore. Only grows in the gnomes' bloody mushroom bed. And only if you're faster than it, layabout.","kitd8y":"Second: embers that never go out. You only get those from a blessed forge.","1lab65w":"Third: a real tear from a truly beautiful nymph. Not a fake one. A REAL one, smart-arse!","ouw1yr":"*presses a vial into his hand* For the tear. Drop it and I'll drop you.","19lqg4e":"And paper? I've still got the filter from the old joint.","1gg4dhe":"Good. The filter already knows the way. Now OUT, layabout, before I change my mind!","1lpl3ph":"*saw* ... *saw* ... *pant* ... *saw*","1nqb615":"Log by log...","d6ose8":"*hammer* ... *hammer* ... Roof on!","w2e842":"THUD!","dd8k4k":"Right. With Grandpa's blessing.","1c4mtyi":"I'll hang the saw back on its nail. Not been this sharp since 1987, blimey.","nh57rm":"And now off to your swamp, the path is clear.","k7e52n":"Hang on. That crow over there is sitting on a really nice straight branch.","16jkpku":"That'd make a perfect fishing rod. If only the beast would get off it...","11qzrws":"Guests","1hqetbv":"Full house. Everyone's waving banknotes. I haven't even got small change.","jd6etx":"As long as these lot are here, Nastya has no time for me. Obviously. They're paying.","168hzv0":"(If it suddenly smelled really sharp in here... they'd definitely leave.)","j77fki":"(The lounge vent... it goes out the back.)","3jynw":"These blokes will stay till dawn. At least.","1gngvld":"Well, Onion? *winks* You still smell a bit of it. Suits you, actually.","1007wpp":"Where has everyone gone? And why does it smell so... funny in here? Who scared off my customers?","wup17v":"No idea. But now you've got time, haven't you?","181xj90":"For the man who pulled me out of the mud? Always. Come to the lounge. On the house – but only for you.","ngkyf7":"*spins round the pole* Well, Petya darling? Full house! The boys pay, I dance.","imvvn8":"Not now, gorgeous. Those lads are rustling banknotes. What are you rustling?","ngkyc8":"Later, darling. When I've emptied their wallets.","1qkohz3":"(The onion. If it gets into the lounge vent... behind the banya...)","uj4tb6":"No money, no lounge. Nothing's free, darling. Unless suddenly nobody's here.","48icfw":"Come back when it's quieter. Maybe a miracle will happen. Miracles cost extra too, mind.","1ec7vvp":"It smells of vegetables in here. And all the guests are gone! Someone's ruined my takings. When I find out who – they're dead.","1fb1ti1":"Oh well. Nastya has time for you now, sweetie. Ask her yourself. And don't think I haven't worked it out.","1uh827n":"A garden. Cabbages the size of prams, onions with the air shimmering above them, and a bed of mushrooms that glitter.","lla3eb":"And Grobnik, looking at me like a bouncer.","9l560z":"To the village","4024un":"Sign: To the garden","1ac2tpk":"HALT, Lanky! Where you sneaking off to?","xujtmp":"That way. To the garden.","1iaieu4":"That's not a garden. That's a warehouse. Gnome gold. Cabbage, onions, mushrooms. All counted. Twice. With invoices.","1d0yn2h":"I only want to look.","1b8atd":"Looking's free. Touching isn't. I'm coming with you. And I'm not taking my eyes off you.","1h6m5s0":"Sign: To the village","12zi4is":"I look. You look. Everyone looks. Nobody touches. Nobody saw nothing.","1gugfyy":"That cabbage is older than you, Lanky. And smarter. And it keeps its mouth shut.","1mjm6rn":"That's not a high bar.","1zduho":"Do you guard the garden at night too?","12x25dz":"At night the cabbage guards itself. Don't ask how.","16u892f":"(I'd better not ask any more.)","1r551q9":"Gnome garden","id8iui":"It smells of earth, cabbage and onion here. In that order, left to right.","14hug2x":"Grobnik is staring. I stare back. He wins.","nkd0mo":"The mushrooms in the bed are glittering. Mushrooms should not glitter.","1xb4gnq":"The garden. Grobnik's already standing there. Of course.","1d9droi":"Back in the gnome garden. The cabbage hasn't grown. I think.","7uthuv":"Item","fwo3ej":"Private dance · on the house","ryq7i":"First person","1q52lrv":"*from very far away* ...Bro...","1ykszts":"Vova?","gv91ny":"(I heard Vova. Here. In the fairytale. That's either a good sign. Or a very bad one.)","1xqgmag":"*closer* ...ther? You having me on?..","mp3z3h":"(Again. Louder this time.)","1acz7ud":"(Does he even notice I'm gone? ...Probably not. Doesn't matter.)","1avuzia":"(...It doesn't.)","l3u2d6":"*very close, as if he were in the room* ...BRO?! Where are you, you get me?!","bqv2ne":"(Coming, Vova. Coming.)","kr185b":"For a cat.","144f1fj":"So he gives up Granny's dentures.","1frrp79":"So Granny gives me tar.","14goi1f":"So Grandpa lets me saw his birches.","3o0yfz":"So I can get into the swamp.","zh6p0z":"So Madame gets a new girl.","8i54tp":"So the miller hands over his \"flour\".","1bs67xf":"So the gnomes let me into their cave.","127suuh":"So the witch helps me.","1rwy6gn":"So I can go home. To my sofa. Where I do nothing.","b2nnrv":"...Marvellous.","1uengf3":"And what do I need tar for? No idea. But in a fairytale you need everything eventually.","10h37pp":"Let me just recap.","1qakdxu":"I'm fishing.","1p6lwp4":"The catfish. Kuzmich got him after all. Respect.","4wuc3b":"...It has fingers. Four of them. With webbing in between.","gu66zx":"And a wristwatch. A \"Slava\". Still ticking, even.","1esxsh5":"And there are blue crumbs in its beard.","1bll42w":"...I didn't see anything. I'm just a bloke who wants to go home.","g1fwzo":"The watch is ticking. The fish isn't. I'm off.","1jsgik8":"Funny eyes, that one. I've seen eyes like that somewhere before... No. I haven't.","ap5fzy":"Did you see him?! On the wall! THE CATFISH! Thirty years! Gaffer-taped him up so he won't fall!","m9ubq3":"Fought like a man. Even swore, I think.","n2uaqx":"(Fish don't swear.)","ltcv9x":"And he nicked my moonshine in the meantime too, the bastard. Must have been him.","dyojqy":"...Definitely.","o4b79a":"A stamp on one sack. A little mushroom. Blue.","158q52l":"Odd logo for a mill. None of my business.","gsmz0n":"A tin behind the bar. It says \"Spice\". Inside: blue crumbs.","14uc3p1":"Hands off, sweetie. That's for regulars. Very regular regulars.","dsvfo1":"Herbs are drying on the windowsill. Chamomile, mint... and something blue.","g71frv":"*from across the way* Thatth for my back! Fifty yearth I've been taking it – and nothing! ...Well, almotht nothing.","1rvm6jd":"(Granny's herbs. No. No, no. ...No.)","155fmm8":"The bottom crate is different. Blue dust in the cracks. And a stamp on it: a little mushroom.","zzgoqk":"I've seen that before. ...Where, though?","1u45wzp":"At full moon we dry the blue sponges for the old woman. On the warm stones. And gossip. Mostly gossip.","53g6r0":"Which old woman?","1asqfuf":"The one with the chicken legs. In return she leaves us alone. And sends a Lanky like you along now and then. Tee-hee, for us to look at.","yimm":"(I wasn't \"sent\". ...Was I?)","cvkn6b":"Doesn't smell like flour. Smells like trouble. On the stamp: a little blue mushroom.","ez15kk":"The crow was here. Grassed you up. You threw an APPLE at her, smart-arse?","psn8om":"She was sitting on my branch.","f5cn3v":"*giggles* Good. That bloody bird's been pecking my head for a hundred years. Now talk.","1a4r1b5":"...You know what, Onion? For three hundred years I felt nothing. Nothing. Just counted banknotes.","1klqc4a":"And then I cry. Because of you. Because of a gnome onion, of all things.","1sxfw5d":"That was the most honest thing that's happened to me since the swamp. ...Thanks, Onion. Don't tell anyone.","1l6hu6o":"(She means it. I think.)","1i0hojr":"Well, Onion? *winks* Come by again. Without vegetables. With money.","dq3ubj":"Sit down. Not the chair on the left, it bites. The other one, smart-arse.","1av35r4":"Before we start. The blue mushrooms. The stamp on the sacks. The dust behind the banya. They're yours, aren't they?","zjd6zy":"Sonny. I'm three hundred years old and I live on chicken legs. You think a house like this feeds itself?","1z11msr":"The gnomes grow, the nymphs dry, the village looks the other way. Everyone takes a little cut. It's called a fairytale economy. Questions?","1wy1f52":"And Vova's joint?","1ej4ab4":"Wastage. Happens in the best of families.","1hfictn":"*pushes a mug towards him* Tea. Nothing in it. This time.","12ht11u":"Most people who sit at this table end up in the oven. You're the first in decades to talk back, smart-arse.","1u36czx":"You could stay, you know. The gnomes need a Lanky. Granny needs someone for her dentures. And I'd... have someone to grumble at, layabout.","h8juwa":"Nobody misses me over there. Vova will only notice I'm gone when his lighter's missing.","1dau5nn":"There you go, then.","ogt3bq":"But here everything hangs on everything. Saw for tar, tar for dentures, dentures for fish. If I stay, I'm just a cog.","1onzczc":"Over there I'm nothing special either. But at least there I'm my own problem.","5thi8s":"...Bloody idiot. *finishes his tea* All right. Roll your joint.","cr4f44":"And if you ever see a blue stamp over there: you were never here. Neither was I. Got it?","2ej2cl":"It's pitch black at the back. Without light I'm not reaching in anywhere. Who knows what reaches back.","1fxcqj":"*holds up the gnome lantern*","1sacgtb":"Green light. And back there, where there was only black before... something glows back. Blue.","a9373q":"Halt, Lanky. The lantern. Signed out, signed in.","1baip0o":"What about it?","3z03sz":"It's inventory. Gnome inventory. Counted every evening. Shortfall's a criminal offence.","1rcpqs3":"*hands it back* Thanks for the light.","x0ald4":"Thanks don't get counted. Lanterns do.","mk06h1":"Characters","uycewk":"Mate from the real world","alxg5b":"My mate. Sofa, CRT telly, always something to smoke. Gave me the joint that started all this.","i322h5":"Sometimes I hear him. From far away, through the wall between the worlds. He's looking for me. I think.","livcq7":"He shouted \"bro\". Vova never says \"bro\". Maybe he does notice when I'm gone.","99lmx2":"Witch in the birch forest","kgddpb":"Lives in a hut on chicken legs. The door is decorative. Guests come through the window, or not at all.","1wiy38c":"Knows the blue mushrooms from Vova's joint. Knows them very well, in fact. Promised me an antidote if I run her errands.","1rr1chg":"The blue mushrooms are her business: gnomes grow, nymphs dry, the village looks away. And she's lonely. Never thought I'd write that about a witch.","1l1htri":"Old man by his burnt-out house","yyja5c":"Stands in front of what's left of his house. Wants moonshine, gives a ladder for it. Fair rate.","3vms7m":"Was a soldier. Soviet army, uniform, medals, the whole works. Then the Soviet Union fell, and with it his pay, his pension and his respect. Suddenly he was standing in a country that no longer existed.","ugdxe2":"Then the house burned down as well. Only the stove was left standing, and he slept next to it, for years. Now he has walls again. Made of birches I sawed. He didn't thank me. He nodded. With him, that's more.","1cfzyj3":"Village street, always at the window","1nlc1ug":"Knows everything about everyone in the village. Tells it, too. Toothless since the priest's cat stole her dentures.","o9zoxe":"Has birch tar for rheumatism, lice and men. Applies all three uses regularly.","m2ebhm":"Dries blue \"herbs\" on her windowsill. Says they're for tea. I don't drink tea at hers any more.","1p8wy05":"Hut by the lake","lh1lfi":"Distils, fishes, swears. Gives nothing away, certainly not voluntarily.","2ly20v":"Has been hunting the same catfish for years. Blames the catfish for everything: lost nets, stolen booze, broken marriage.","1uv0qy5":"Finally got him. The catfish hangs on his hut, with webbing between its fingers and a gold watch on its wrist. Kuzmich thinks that's normal. I saw nothing.","kgtbwu":"Boss of the banya","1reclg0":"Runs the banya. Steam, dancing, vodka. Looking for new girls and calls anyone who pays \"sweetie\".","7zzn5d":"Has a list: pretty, loves to dance, cheeky, wants out. I brought her a nymph from the swamp. She didn't even ask how.","1qgcxao":"In the back yard there are crates stacked up with blue dust and a mushroom stamp. Zinaida doesn't just sell vodka. I don't ask. I want to keep the voucher.","1754p89":"Nymph, now a dancer at the banya","bchnib":"Came out of the swamp, now dances on the pole. Winks as if she knows more than you. She does.","dae7pu":"Three hundred years in the swamp. Has seen merchants, soldiers and a priest come and go. Considers the banya a promotion.","1rw66nu":"Hadn't felt anything for three hundred years. Then along came a gnome onion and me. She cried and laughed at the same time. Since then she calls me \"Onion\". I think it's a term of endearment.","i9t1xl":"Gnome, guardian of the cave","1m2cwew":"Stands in front of the cave and lets nobody in. Wants \"flour\". Says \"trade secret\" more often than is good for him.","1huo6qq":"Sniffed the \"flour\" like a customs dog on holiday. Gave me his lantern for it. On loan.","gc2dfh":"Counts the lanterns every evening. He doesn't count thank-yous. The gnome realm is accountancy with beards.","f867kq":"The Miller","a8e9lw":"Voice from the mill. Wants a bride. Allegedly grinds flour.","161tl9z":"Gave me three sacks of \"flour\". For a private-dance voucher. The flour doesn't smell like flour.","dwb54t":"There's a blue mushroom stamp on his sacks. The mill isn't a mill. It's a warehouse.","l944zz":"Priest of the wooden church","1si9co":"Sleeps in the hay behind the banya. Since 1993. A note on his church says: \"Priest in town\".","1yh4xbj":"Only wanted to rest his eyes after a beer. With a little blue mushroom \"to relax\", from the old woman in the woods. Thirty years of relaxation.","1idzj9r":"Waters down his holy water with vodka. \"For shelf life.\" The cat sits on the altar now and has been in the congregation longer than he has.","1hqft0d":"Big, sooty, honest. The only one in the village who wants money for work and not favours.","1s4tllu":"Sharpened Grandpa's saw. Now I owe him. With him that's not a feeling, it's a chalk mark on the wall. His favourite phrase: \"Chalk at the ready.\" Says it whenever he puts something on the slate. So, constantly.","1vy2rcc":"His forge had been burning unblessed since 1993 because the priest was \"in town\". Now it glows blessed and smells faintly of vodka. He smiled for the first time.","rn5s8i":"Birch forest, on the branch","c4q7ep":"Sits on the best branch in the forest and defends it like a dacha.","ex5qtz":"Got hit by an apple. From me. Had to be done.","hh6z6t":"Grassed me up to Baba Yaga. Crows are the secret police of the forest.","4pkw54":"Haven't met anyone yet. Just as well, really.","quph13":"Notebook: something new about a character (key C)","1gdbhhi":"Petya and the Cursed Birch Forest","1sl08td":"Painting the forest...","fxh0tx":"an adventure among birches, swamps and bad decisions","1942lsv":"Pockets – click an item to look at it","i2piau":"on","brf73s":"off","hzlkau":"On","133q2xk":"Off","no6co6":"Petya only","pmt3ah":"All characters","1of5gvb":"Automatic","bqpurh":"empty","1mpgp6c":"nothing yet","540b06":"Auto","j4z771":"Pause","1q9i7rd":"News","6tqk79":"Close (ESC)","f375z3":"Sort the blue-tinged mushroom bits into the bowl. Only those!","1oi0eqm":"The bowl is contaminated! Sort it all again.","l5id3v":"Next step","1mfwn8a":"Nothing open right now.","1m2u3wi":"Pick a slot.","teto13":"Play first, then save.","10k4la5":"… There's more to this one.","14bon50":"Language · Sprache · Язык","1cd3umw":"*breathes into your ear* Comfy, gorgeous? I can feel something down there. ...Hope it's your wallet.","1er1396":"*GULP*","15b1k8n":"1993?! ...What year is it, my son? Never mind – the Lord doesn't count years.","11tcjxo":"1993?! I only wanted to close my eyes after a beer... Well, I'm well rested. Every cloud."};
